hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"601","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us that he heard Amr ibn Aws al-Thaqafi saying: I heard Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: The most beloved fasting to Allah is the fasting of Dawud; he would fast a day and break a day; and the most beloved prayer to Allah is the prayer of Dawud; he would sleep half the night, stand a third of it, and sleep a sixth of it."
"602","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, saying: I heard Abu al-Abbas the blind saying: I heard Abdullah ibn Amr saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me in my house and said: Have I not been told that you stand the night and fast the day? I said: I do that. He said: Do not do it; for your eyes have a right upon you, and your self has a right upon you, and your family has a right upon you; and if you do that, your eye will grow weary and your self will grow jaded; so stand and sleep, and fast and break."
"603","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Amr narrated to us, saying: Abu Qabus, freedman of Abdullah ibn Amr, informed me that he heard Abdullah ibn Amr saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The merciful will be shown mercy by the Most Merciful; show mercy to those on earth, and those in heaven will show mercy to you."
"604","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, saying: Abu Qabus informed me that he heard Abdullah ibn Amr saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Kinship is a branch of the Most Merciful; whoever joins it, Allah joins him, and whoever cuts it, Allah cuts him."
"605","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Bashir ibn Sulayman Abu Ismail narrated to us, from Mujahid ibn Jabr, that Abdullah ibn Amr ordered a sheep slaughtered and said to his steward: Did you give anything to our Jewish neighbor? For I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Gabriel, peace be upon him, kept enjoining me concerning the neighbor until I thought he would make him an heir."
"606","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Bashir ibn Sulayman Abu Ismail and Fitr ibn Khalifa the tailor narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Abdullah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The joiner is not the requiter; but the joiner is the one who, when his kinship is cut, joins it."
"607","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, saying: I heard al-Sha'bi saying: A man came to Abdullah ibn Amr while I was with him, stepping over people's necks until he sat before him, then said: Narrate to me something you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and do not narrate to me from the two just ones. Abdullah ibn Amr said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The Muslim is the one from whose tongue and hand Muslims are safe; and the emigrant is the one who abandons evil — or he said: what Allah forbade."
"608","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, and Ibn Abi Khalid narrated it to us, from al-Sha'bi, from Abdullah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — and he did not mention the two just ones."
"609","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: We heard it from Dawud ibn Shabur and Ya'qub ibn Ata, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather Abdullah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning a treasure a man found: If you found it in an inhabited village or on a frequented road, announce it; and if you found it in a pre-Islamic ruin, or in an uninhabited village, or off a frequented road, then concerning it and buried treasure is the fifth."
"610","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Dawud ibn Shabur and Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us — and I remember the hadith of Ibn Ajlan better — from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather Abdullah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The arrogant will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection like tiny ants in the form of men, with all humiliation covering them; they will be driven to a prison in the Fire called Bulas, with the fire of fires covering them, given to drink of the mire of al-Khabal, the juices of the people of the Fire."
"611","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Wahb ibn Jabir, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It suffices a man as sin to neglect those he feeds."
"612","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Al-Zuhri narrated to us, saying: I heard Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf saying: I heard Muawiya ibn Abi Sufyan on the day of Ashura, while upon the pulpit of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), having taken from his sleeve a lock of hair, saying: Where are your scholars, O people of Medina? I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbidding the like of this, saying: The Children of Israel were destroyed only when their women adopted them."
"613","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Al-Zuhri narrated to us, saying: I heard Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman saying: I heard Muawiya ibn Abi Sufyan on the day of Ashura, upon the pulpit of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I am fasting, so whoever of you wishes to fast it, let him fast it."
"614","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us that he heard Muhammad ibn Hayyan narrating from Abdullah ibn Muhayriz, who said: I heard Muawiya ibn Abi Sufyan saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not race me in bowing and prostration, for I have grown heavy; whenever I precede you in bowing, you catch me when I rise, and whenever I precede you in prostration, you catch me when I rise."
"615","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hayyan, from Ibn Muhayriz, from Muawiya, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the like of it, except that he said: For I have grown heavy."
"616","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Amr narrated to us, saying: I heard Wahb ibn Munabbih in his house in Sana — and he fed me of a walnut in his house — narrating from his brother, from Muawiya ibn Abi Sufyan, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not press insistently in asking; for by Allah, none of you asks me for anything and the asking draws it out of me so that I give it to him while I dislike it, and it is blessed for him in what I gave him."
"617","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Hisham ibn Hujayr narrated to us, from Tawus, who said: I heard Ibn Abbas saying: This is a proof against Muawiya in his statement: I trimmed the hair from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a Bedouin razor at Marwa — Ibn Abbas says: when he forbade mut'a."
"618","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Talha ibn Yahya narrated to us, from his uncle Isa ibn Talha, that he heard Muawiya ibn Abi Sufyan saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When the caller says: Allah is greatest, Allah is greatest, say: Allah is greatest, Allah is greatest. And when he says: I bear witness there is no god but Allah, say: And I bear witness. And when he says: I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, say: And I bear witness. Then remain silent."
"619","Sufyan said: And Mujammi' ibn Yahya al-Ansari narrated to us, from Abu Umama ibn Sahl, from Muawiya, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the like of it."
"620","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Al-Zuhri narrated to us more than once — I bear witness to you of it — saying: Salim ibn Abdullah informed me, from his father, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, and Umar walking in front of the funeral."
"621","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from his father, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon the pulpit saying: Whoever of you comes to Friday, let him bathe."
"622","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the like of it."
"623","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Ismail ibn Umayya and Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the like of it."
"624","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Salim, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bilal calls the adhan at night, so eat and drink until you hear the adhan of Ibn Umm Maktum."
"625","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Salim, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the wife of one of you asks his permission to go to the mosque, let him not forbid her. Sufyan said: They hold it is at night."
"626","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Al-Zuhri narrated to us alone, with no one with me nor with him, saying: Salim ibn Abdullah informed me, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sells a slave who has wealth, his wealth belongs to the one who sold him unless the buyer stipulates it; and whoever sells palm trees after they have been pollinated, their fruit belongs to the seller unless the buyer stipulates it."
"627","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Al-Zuhri narrated to us, saying: Salim ibn Abdullah informed me, from his father, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he began the prayer raise his hands level with his shoulders, and when he intended to bow, and after he raised his head from bowing; and he would not raise between the two prostrations."
"628","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, saying: I heard Zayd ibn Waqid narrating from Nafi: that Abdullah ibn Umar, when he saw a man praying without raising his hands each time he lowered and raised, would pelt him until he raised his hands."
"629","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Al-Zuhri narrated to us, saying: Salim narrated to me, from his father, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when travel pressed him, combine Maghrib and Isha."
"630","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Salim, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no envy except in two: a man to whom Allah gave the Quran and he stands with it through hours of the night and hours of the day; and a man to whom Allah gave wealth and he spends of it through hours of the night and hours of the day."
"631","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not leave fire in your houses when you sleep."
"632","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Al-Zuhri narrated to us — by Allah — from Salim, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Five animals: there is no sin upon whoever kills them, in the sacred state or outside it: the crow, the kite, the scorpion, the mouse, and the vicious dog. It was said to Sufyan: Ma'mar narrates it from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, from Aisha; so he said: Al-Zuhri narrated to us, by Allah, from Salim, from his father; he did not mention Urwa, from Aisha."
"633","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Salim, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Kill snakes, and the striped one and the tailless one, for they seek eyesight and cause miscarriage. He said: And Abdullah would kill every snake he found, until Abu Lubaba — or Zayd ibn al-Khattab — saw him pursuing a snake and said: Those of the houses have been forbidden. Sufyan said: Al-Zuhri would always say in it: Zayd or Abu Lubaba."
"634","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Salim, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ill omen is in three: in the horse, the woman, and the house. It was said to Sufyan: But they say in it: from Hamza; Sufyan said: I never heard al-Zuhri mention Hamza in this hadith at all."
"635","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Salim, from his father: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling fruit until its ripeness appears, and forbade selling fruit for dates. Ibn Umar said: And Zayd ibn Thabit informed me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted the sale of araya."
"636","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Salim, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of Medina enter ihram from Dhu al-Hulayfa, the people of Syria from al-Juhfa, and the people of Najd from Qarn. And he mentioned to me, though I did not hear it: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And the people of Yemen from Yalamlam."
"637","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from his father, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard Umar swearing by his father, so he said: Verily Allah forbids you to swear by your fathers. Umar said: By Allah, I never swore by it after that, neither deliberately nor transmitting. Al-Humaydi said: Sufyan said: I heard Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, freedman of the family of Talha — learned in Arabic — saying: Nor transmitting: transmitting it from another, informing of him that he swore by it."
"638","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Salim, from his father: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a man of the Ansar admonishing his brother concerning modesty, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Modesty is of faith."
"639","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Salim, from his father: that a man stood to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him what clothing the pilgrim in ihram wears. He said: He wears no shirt, no turban, no trousers, no hooded cloak, no garment touched by saffron or wars, and no leather socks, except for one who finds no sandals; whoever finds no sandals, let him cut them until they are below the ankles."
"640","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Ismail ibn Umayya, Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, Ayyub ibn Musa, and Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the like of it, except that they said: Nor a garment touched by saffron or wars, at the end of the hadith."
"641","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: I heard al-Zuhri, and he narrated to us from Salim ibn Abdullah, from his father, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The night prayer is two by two; then if you fear dawn, make it odd with one."
"642","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: And Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Tawus, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the like of it."
"643","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Abi Labid narrated to us, from Abu Salama, from Abdullah ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the like of it."
"644","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Dinar narrated to us, saying: I heard Ibn Umar saying: I heard a man asking the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while upon the pulpit: How does one of us pray at night? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two by two; then if you fear dawn, make it odd with one, which makes odd for you what passed. Sufyan said: And this is the best of them."
"645","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Salim, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever keeps a dog — except a hunting dog or a livestock dog — two qirats are deducted from his reward each day."
"646","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Dinar narrated to us, saying: I went with Ibn Umar to Banu Muawiya, and their dogs barked at us, so Ibn Umar said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever keeps a dog except a hunting dog or a livestock dog, two qirats are deducted from his reward each day."
"647","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Salim, from his father, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I saw Laylat al-Qadr on such-and-such night; so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I see your dreams agree, so seek it in the last ten, in its odd nights, or in the remaining seven. Sufyan said: The doubt is from me, not from al-Zuhri."
"648","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Al-Zuhri narrated to us, saying: Abu Bakr ibn Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Umar informed me that he heard his grandfather Abdullah ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you eats, let him eat with his right hand; and when he drinks, let him drink with his right hand; for Satan eats with his left and drinks with his left."
"649","Sufyan said: And I heard Ma'mar narrating it afterwards from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, so I said to him: O Abu Urwa, it is only from Abu Bakr; so Ma'mar said: We presented it. And Sufyan would sometimes say: This is of what we presented."
"650","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to me, saying: My father sent me to Abdullah ibn Umar, and I entered upon him without permission, so he taught me, saying: When you come, seek permission; and when permitted, greet when you enter. And the son of his son, Abdullah ibn Waqid ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, passed with a new garment trailing it, so he said to him: O my son, raise your waist-wrapper; for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah does not look at one who trails his garment in pride."
"651","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: The keeper of this house in al-Jarr, Umayya ibn Hafs ibn Muhallaf, freedman of the family of Majida, narrated to us, saying: I heard Muslim ibn Yannaq saying: I was with Abdullah ibn Umar at the door of the house of Abdullah ibn Khalid ibn Asid, when a youth passed with his waist-wrapper lowered, so Ibn Umar said to him: Raise your waist-wrapper; for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah does not look at one who trails his garment in pride."
"652","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Abi Labid narrated to us — of the worshippers of Medina — saying: I heard Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman saying: I heard Ibn Umar saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Let not the Bedouins overcome you in the name of your prayer, for it is only Isha; they call it Atama because they delay milking the camels — or he said: with the camels. Sufyan said: Thus Ibn Abi Labid said it, with doubt."
"653","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Dinar narrated to us — we heard it from him repeated and set forth — saying: Ibn Umar heard saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling wala and gifting it. It was said to him: Shu'ba made Abdullah swear to it; he said: But we did not make him swear; we heard it from him many times. Then Sufyan laughed."
"654","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Ibn Dinar — meaning Abdullah ibn Dinar — narrated to us that he heard Ibn Umar saying: We pledged to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hearing and obedience, and when we pledged to him he would dictate to us, saying: As much as you are able."
"655","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan and Salih ibn Qudama narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Abdullah ibn Umar, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the spiny-tailed lizard, so he said: I neither eat it nor forbid it."
"656","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Hisham ibn Urwa narrated to us, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the like of it."
"657","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Salih ibn Kaysan narrated to us, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when returning from a hajj, umra, or raid and rising upon high ground, would say: There is no god but Allah, alone without partner; to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things capable; returning, if Allah wills, repentant, worshipping, to our Lord praising; Allah kept His promise, aided His servant, and alone defeated the Confederates."
"658","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the like of it, except he did not say: If Allah wills. It was said to Sufyan: Is in it: prostrating? He said: How likely, but I do not remember it."
"659","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan and Salih ibn Qudama al-Jumahi al-Madani narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Dinar narrated to us that he heard Ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two shall not converse privately to the exclusion of the third."
"660","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, better than it, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two shall not converse privately to the exclusion of the third. He said: And when Ibn Umar wished to converse privately while they were three, he would call a fourth."
"661","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, that Ibn Umar said to Yahya ibn Hayyan: Do you not see killing as a thing, when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two shall not converse privately to the exclusion of the third. [flag: Arabic abrupt; connection of killing clause garbled — literal kept]"
"662","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan and Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, saying: Muslim ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us: Ali ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Mu'awi informed me, saying: I prayed beside Ibn Umar and turned the pebbles, and when he finished he said: Do not turn the pebbles, for turning pebbles is of Satan; and do as you saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) doing. I said: How did you see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) doing? So he placed his right hand upon his right thigh — and Abu Bakr closed three fingers and raised the forefinger — and placed his left hand upon his left thigh and spread it."
"663","Sufyan said: And Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated it to us from Muslim, then when I met Muslim he narrated it to me, adding in it: And it is the fly-whisk of Satan; none is unmindful while saying thus — and al-Humaydi raised his finger. Muslim said: And a man narrated to me that he saw the prophets depicted in a church in Syria in their prayer saying thus — and al-Humaydi raised his finger."
"664","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Musa ibn Uqba narrated to me, saying: I heard Salim ibn Abdullah narrating from his father, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned of the waist-wrapper what he mentioned, Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, my waist-wrapper slips from one side. He said: You are not of them."
"665","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, and Amr narrated from Tawus, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the like of it."
"666","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: And Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id, from a man called Ubayd ibn Jurayj who used to accompany Ibn Umar, that he asked Abdullah ibn Umar, saying: I saw you doing something I saw none of your companions doing: I saw you not entering ihram until your mount rises with you; I saw you wearing these tanned-leather sandals and performing ablution in them; I saw you touching of the House only these two corners; and I saw you dyeing your beard yellow. Ibn Umar answered him, saying: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) not entering ihram until his mount rose with him; I saw him wearing these tanned-leather sandals and performing ablution in them; I saw him touching of this House only these two corners; and I saw him dyeing his beard yellow."
"667","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us more than seventy years ago, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: Umar came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have acquired wealth the like of which I never acquired, the hundred shares at Khaybar, and I wish to draw near to Allah through it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Umar, immobilize the principal and devote its yield to charity."
"668","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning the people of Al-Hijr: Do not enter upon these people who were punished except weeping; if you are not weeping then do not enter upon them, for I fear that what befell them may befall you."
"669","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: I came to Nafi, and he set down a satchel and I sat upon it, and he dictated to me on my tablets, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When two parties trade, each of them has the option so long as they have not separated, unless their sale is on condition of an option. He said: And Ibn Umar, when he made a purchase and wanted it to be binding, would walk a little then return."
"670","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Dinar narrated to us that he heard Abdullah ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two sellers each have the option so long as they have not separated, unless their sale is on condition of an option; and if it is on condition of an option then it has become binding."
"671","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Dinar narrated to us that he heard Abdullah ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a Jew greets you, he only says: As-sam be upon you, so say: And upon you. Abdullah ibn Dinar said: There was a Jewish man who then became Muslim, and he would greet Ibn Umar, and when Ibn Umar returned his greeting he would add nothing beyond saying: And upon you; so the man would say: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, I have become Muslim, yet he would add nothing beyond saying: And upon you."
"672","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Dinar narrated to us that he heard Ibn Umar say: Umar asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): May one of us sleep while in a state of major impurity? He said: Yes, when he has performed ablution, and he may eat if he wishes."
"673","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Dinar narrated to us that he heard Ibn Umar say: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) come to Quba walking and riding every Saturday, and I saw Ibn Umar come to Quba riding and walking every Saturday."
"674","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Uqbah narrated to us, he said: I heard Salim ibn Abdullah say: I heard Ibn Umar say: This is Al-Bayda about which you tell lies against the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); by Allah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only entered ihram from beside the mosque of Dhul-Hulayfah."
"675","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Here I am, O Allah, here I am; here I am, there is no partner for You, here I am; indeed praise and blessing belong to You, and dominion; there is no partner for You. He said: And Abdullah ibn Umar would add, saying: Here I am, here I am, here I am, and at Your service; here I am, and good is in Your hands. This is what Sufyan used to say: Here I am, and desire and deed are directed to You."
"676","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Asim ibn Muhammad al-Umari narrated to us, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If people knew what I know about being alone, no rider would ever travel by night alone."
"677","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: that Munqidh was struck on his head in the pre-Islamic period with a wound reaching the brain, which affected his tongue, and when he bargained he would be deceived in the transaction. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Bargain, and say: No deception, and you then have the option for three days. Ibn Umar said: So I heard him bargain, saying: No khidhaba [flag: source reads la khidhabah here, apparently for la khilabah, no deception]."
"678","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will find people like a hundred camels among which there is scarcely a riding camel."
"679","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you should make a man get up from his seat and then sit in it; rather make room and spread out."
"680","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Sadaqah ibn Yasar narrated to us, from Nafi: that Ibn Umar would pass by a tree between Makkah and Madinah under which the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to shade himself, and he would carry water for it from a distant place until he poured it beneath it."
"681","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: I heard Ubaydullah ibn Umar say many times, he said: I heard Nafi say: I heard Abdullah ibn Umar say: I do not forbid anyone to pray at whatever hour he wishes of night or day, but I only do as I saw my companions do; and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not deliberately time your prayer for the rising of the sun or its setting. It was said to Sufyan: This is reported from Hisham. He said: I never heard Hisham mention it at all."
"682","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Nafi, who said: I saw Ibn Umar standing on Al-Safa in a place, and I think, by Allah, that he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) standing in it."
"683","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, he said: We asked Ibn Umar about a man who performed umrah and circumambulated the House seven times but did not go between Al-Safa and Al-Marwah: may he approach his wife? Ibn Umar said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and circumambulated the House seven times, prayed two rakahs behind the Station, and went between Al-Safa and Al-Marwah, and said: Allah said: Indeed you have in the Messenger of Allah an excellent example."
"684","Amr said: We asked Jabir ibn Abdullah, and he said: She should not draw near to him until he goes between Al-Safa and Al-Marwah."
"685","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, he said: It was said to Ibn Umar: Abu Nuhayk, a man of the people of Makkah, eats a great deal of food. Ibn Umar said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer eats with one intestine, while the disbeliever eats with seven intestines. The man then said: As for me, I believe in Allah and His Messenger."
"686","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If a slave is owned between two men and one of them frees his share, then if he is wealthy it shall be assessed against him at the highest value, or he said: at a just value with neither undervaluation nor excess, then he compensates his partner for his share, and then he is fully freed. Sufyan said: Amr used to doubt about it in this manner."
"687","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, he said: I heard Said ibn Jubayr say: I heard Ibn Umar say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say to the two who invoked mutual curses: Your reckoning is with Allah; one of you is lying; you have no way to her. He said: O Messenger of Allah, my wealth, my wealth. He said: You have no claim to wealth; if you told the truth about her, it is for what you made lawful of her private part, and if you lied about her, that is even further removed for you from it."
"688","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani narrated to us that he heard Said ibn Jubayr say: I asked Ibn Umar, saying: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, a man invoked mutual curses against his wife. Ibn Umar said to me with his hand, like this with his index and middle fingers: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) separated the two brothers of Banu Ajlan and said: Allah knows that one of you is lying, so is either of you repentant? Sufyan said: Ayyub had first narrated it to us in the gathering of Amr, then Amr narrated this hadith of his, and Ayyub said to him: You, O Abu Muhammad, narrate it better than I."
"689","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, he said: I heard Ismail al-Shaybani say: I sold what was on the tops of my palm trees for a hundred wasqs of dates; if it exceeded, it was theirs, and if it fell short, it was upon them. So I asked Ibn Umar about that, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that, except that he permitted al-araya."
"690","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr narrated to us before we met al-Zuhri, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray two rakahs after Friday prayer, and I saw him pray two rakahs before Zhuhr and two after it, two after Maghrib, and two after Isha. Ibn Umar said: And it was mentioned to me, though I did not see it, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray two rakahs when dawn broke for him."
"691","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Ibn Umar, who said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and I was on a difficult young camel belonging to Umar; it would overpower me and advance ahead of the people, so Umar would restrain it and turn it back, then it would advance again and Umar would restrain it and turn it back. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Umar: Sell it to me. He said: It is yours, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Sell it to me. So he sold it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is yours, O Abdullah ibn Umar, do with it what you wish."
"692","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn Musa narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a ring of gold, then threw it away, and took a ring of silver whose stone was of it, and he placed its stone toward the inside of his palm, and engraved upon it: Muhammad, Messenger of Allah; and he forbade anyone to engrave upon it. It is the one that fell from Muayqib into the well of Aris."
"693","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Najih narrated to us, from Mujahid, who said: I accompanied Ibn Umar to Al-Thaniyyah, and I did not hear him narrate from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except one hadith. He said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the heart of a palm tree was brought, and he said: I know a tree whose likeness is like that of the Muslim man. It occurred to me that it was the date palm, and I wanted to speak, then I looked and I was the youngest of the people, so I kept silent. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is the date palm."
"694","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, who said: Umar said to me: That you had said it would be dearer to me than such-and-such, or he said: than red camels."
"695","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn Musa, Ubaydullah ibn Umar, and Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani narrated to us; they heard Nafi say: Ibn Umar entered ihram for umrah when he set out from Madinah, saying: If I am prevented, I shall do as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did. When he reached Al-Bayda he said: Their matter is but one; I call you to witness that I have obligated Hajj along with my umrah. He said: Then he arrived at Makkah, circumambulated the House seven times, prayed two rakahs behind the Station, and went between Al-Safa and Al-Marwah, then said: Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do. Ayyub ibn Musa added in the hadith: When he reached Qudayd he bought a sacrificial animal there and drove it."
"696","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn Musa narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a striped silk cloak on Utarid and disliked it for him and forbade him from it. Then he gave Umar the like of it as a gift. He said: O Messenger of Allah, you said concerning the cloak of Utarid what you said, yet you give me this as a gift? He said: I did not give it to you to wear; I only gave it to you to clothe women with it."
"697","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Najih narrated to us, he said: I heard Ismail ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Dhuayb al-Asadi say: We went out with Ibn Umar to Al-Hima. When the sun set we were reluctant to say to him: Dismount and pray. When the twilight disappeared he dismounted and led us in Maghrib, three rakahs, then gave salutations, and prayed Isha two rakahs, then turned to us and said: Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do. Sufyan said: Ibn Abi Najih, when he narrated this hadith, often would not say in it: When the twilight disappeared; he would say: When the whiteness of the horizon went and the darkness of Isha came, he dismounted and prayed. So I said to him about it, and he said: Ismail only said: The twilight disappeared; but I dislike it, so I say it thus, because Mujahid narrated to us that al-shafaq is the daytime. Sufyan said: So I narrate it thus one time, and thus another time."
"698","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Najih narrated to us, from his father, from a man: that a man asked Ibn Umar about fasting the Day of Arafah. Ibn Umar said: I performed Hajj with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he did not fast it; I performed Hajj with Abu Bakr and he did not fast it; I performed Hajj with Umar and he did not fast it; I performed Hajj with Uthman and he did not fast it; and I do not fast it, nor command it, nor forbid it."
"699","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr narrated to us, from Abu al-Thawrayn al-Jumahi, who said: I asked Ibn Umar about fasting the Day of Arafah, and he forbade me."
"700","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Umayyah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you should milk the livestock of another man without his permission; would one of you like someone to come to the door of his storeroom, break its door, and scatter his food? Their stored food is but in the udders of their livestock."
"701","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Umayyah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) held a race between horses; he sent what had been trained of them from Al-Hafya to the mosque of Banu Zurayq, and sent what had not been trained from Thaniyyat al-Wada to the mosque of Banu Zurayq. Ibn Umar said: And I was among those who raced, and my horse plunged with me into a ravine and threw me."
"702","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cut down and burned the property of Banu al-Nadir. Sufyan said: I did not hear it from him [flag: Sufyan states he did not hear this directly from Musa]."
"703","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Umayyah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met Umar while he was on his journey saying: By my father, by my father. He said: Verily Allah forbids you to swear by your fathers; whoever would swear, let him swear by Allah or be silent."
"704","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dispatched a detachment, and they met the enemy and the people fled in rout. We came to Madinah and hid ourselves in it, saying: O Messenger of Allah, we are the deserters. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Rather you are those who return to the fight, and I am your support."
"705","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Suqah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ali, that he heard him say: Ibn Umar, when he heard something, would neither add to it nor subtract from it, nor go beyond it to something else, nor fall short of it. Ubayd ibn Umayr narrated, while Ibn Umar was seated, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of the hypocrite is like a sheep between two flocks, butted by this one once and by that one once. Ibn Umar said: Between the two resting places of sheep. It was said to him: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, between the two resting places and between the two flocks are the same. But Ibn Umar insisted upon nothing but the two resting places, as he had heard it."
"706","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani narrated to us, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of the offspring of the offspring in the womb."
"707","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears and says: If Allah, the Exalted, wills, has made an exception."
"708","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani narrated to us, he said: I heard Nafi say: I heard Ibn Umar say: Umar had a vow of itikaf for a night in the Sacred Mosque in the pre-Islamic period, so he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he commanded him to observe itikaf for a night and fulfill his vow."
"709","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Makkah on the day of the Conquest upon the camel of Usamah ibn Zayd until he made it kneel in the courtyard of the Kabah. Then he called for Uthman ibn Talhah for the key, and he went to his mother, but she refused to give it to him. He said: You shall surely give it to me, or the sword shall surely come out from my loins. So she gave him the key, and he opened the door. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered, along with Usamah ibn Zayd, Bilal, and Uthman ibn Talhah, and they closed the door upon them for a while. I was a strong young man, so I hastened to the door when it was opened, and Bilal met me. I said: O Bilal, where did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray? He said: Between the two front pillars; and I forgot to ask him how many he prayed."
"710","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Misar narrated to us, he said: I heard Simak al-Hanafi say: I asked Ibn Umar about prayer in the House, and he said: Pray in it, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in it; and another will come who will forbid you, so do not obey him. So I went to Ibn Abbas and asked him, and he said: Face all of it and do not leave any part of it behind you."
"711","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent us on a detachment toward Najd, and our shares reached twelve camels, and we were given an extra camel each as spoil."
"712","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi, who said: Ibn Umar was afflicted with cold while in ihram, and he said to Nafi: Throw something over me. So I cast a hooded cloak over him, and he became angry and said: You cast it over me though I told you that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade it?"
"713","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned a Jewish man and a Jewish woman. Ibn Umar said: And I saw him shielding her with his hand."
"714","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, he said: I heard Nafi say: I heard Ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No Muslim man who has wealth concerning which a bequest is due should let two nights pass except that his bequest is written with him."
"715","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us: Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man declares his brother a disbeliever, one of them has surely incurred it."
"716","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Quran should not be carried on a journey to the land of the enemy, lest the enemy seize it."
"717","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi: that Ibn Umar called the iqamah for prayer at Dajnan on a rainy night, then said: Pray in your dwellings. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command his caller to announce on a rainy night, or a cold windy night: Verily pray in your dwellings."
"718","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The charity of breaking the fast is a sa of barley or a sa of dates. Ibn Umar said: Then when Muawiyah came, the people equated half a sa of wheat with a sa of barley. Nafi said: And Ibn Umar used to give the charity of breaking the fast on behalf of the young and old of his household, the free and the slave."
"719","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Zayd ibn Judan narrated to us that he heard al-Qasim ibn Rabiah report, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of the Conquest of Makkah, upon the steps of the Kabah: Praise be to Allah who fulfilled His promise, aided His servant, and alone routed the confederates. Verily the slain of deliberate killing resembling error, with a whip or a stick, entails a hundred camels, aggravated, among them forty pregnant she-camels carrying their young in their bellies. Verily every distinction of the pre-Islamic period, whether blood or wealth, is beneath these two feet of mine, except the custodianship of the House or the providing of water to the pilgrims, for I have confirmed them for their people as they were."
"720","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Suayr ibn al-Khums al-Tamimi narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Islam is built upon five: testimony that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, establishing prayer, giving zakah, fasting the month of Ramadan, and Hajj to the House. Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us once from Suayr and Misar, then I never heard Sufyan mention Misar after that [flag: source contains two reports, numbered 720 and 721 in print, merged into this csv row]."
"721","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, he said: Ibn Umar bought emaciated camels from a partner of Nawwas. When Nawwas came he said to his partner: From whom did you sell them? He described to him the appearance of Ibn Umar, and he said: Woe to you, that is Ibn Umar. So Nawwas came to Ibn Umar and said: My partner sold you emaciated camels, and he did not know you. He said: Then take them. When he went to take them he said: Leave them; we are content with the decree of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): There is no contagion. Sufyan said: Amr said: Nawwas used to sit with Ibn Umar and would make him laugh. One day he said: I wish Abu Qubays were gold for me. Ibn Umar said to him: What would you do with it? He said: I would die upon it. So Ibn Umar laughed."
"722","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu al-Abbas the blind say: I heard Abdullah ibn Umar ibn al-Khattab say: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) besieged the people of Taif, he said: We shall return, God willing, tomorrow. They said: O Messenger of Allah, will you depart before conquering it? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then go forth to battle tomorrow, God willing, the Exalted. He said: So they went forth to battle, and they suffered severe wounds. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We shall return tomorrow, God willing. It was as if they desired that and inclined to it. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed."
"723","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Maysarah narrated to us, from Tawus, who said: I was seated with Abdullah ibn Umar, and a man came and said: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid fermented drink from the earthen jar and the gourd? He said: Yes."
"724","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the pulpit, so I hastened to him to hear what he said, but I did not reach him until he descended. I asked the people: What did he say? They said: He forbade the gourd and the pitch-coated vessel."
"725","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Kab ibn Ujrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by me at Al-Hudaybiyah while I was kindling a fire under a pot or a cauldron, and lice were falling from my head. He said: Do your vermin trouble you, O Kab? I said: Yes. He said: Then shave your head, and offer a sacrifice, or fast three days, or feed a faraq among six poor persons."
"726","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Najih narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Kab ibn Ujrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it, except that he said: Kindling under a pot, and said: And slaughter a sheep."
"727","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Kab ibn Ujrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught us the prayer upon him, saying: Say: O Allah, bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad as You blessed Ibrahim and the family of Ibrahim; indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious. O Allah, bestow bounty upon Muhammad and the family of Muhammad as You bestowed bounty upon Ibrahim and the family of Ibrahim; indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious."
"728","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: And Abd al-Karim Abu Umayyah narrated to me, from Mujahid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Kab ibn Ujrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"729","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu Yafur al-Abdi narrated to us, he said: I went to Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa and asked him about eating locusts. He said: I took part in six or seven expeditions with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we used to eat locusts."
"730","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani narrated to us, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa say: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and he said to a man: Dismount and mix sawiq for me. He said: It is still daytime, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Dismount and mix for me. He said: It is still daytime, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Dismount and mix. So he dismounted and mixed for him, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drank. Then he gestured with his hand toward the east and said: When you see the night approaching from here, the fasting person has broken his fast."
"731","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani narrated to us, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade drinking from the green jar and the white jar. Sufyan said: And a third, which I have forgotten."
"732","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us: Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani narrated to us, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa say: We seized donkeys on the day of Khaybar outside the village and slaughtered them, and the pots were boiling with them, when the caller of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called out: Overturn the pots with what is in them. So we overturned them while they were seething. Abu Ishaq said: I met Said ibn Jubayr and mentioned that to him, and he said: Those were but donkeys that eat filth, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade them."
"733","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Yazid Abu Khalid al-Dalani and Misar ibn Kidam narrated to us, from Ibrahim al-Saksaki, from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa: that a man said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Teach me, O Messenger of Allah, something I may say that suffices me instead of the Quran. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Say: Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is Most Great. Sufyan said: I know only that he said, he said: And there is no power nor strength except through Allah."
"734","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Muslim al-Hajari narrated to us: that he saw Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa at the funeral of a daughter of his, upon a mule being led with him, saying to the guide: Where am I in relation to her? When it was said to him: In front of her, he said: Stop. He said: And I saw him, when he prayed over her, magnify Allah four times, then stand for a while, and the people prompted him with tasbih, then he gave salutations. Then he said: Did you think I would add to four, when I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) magnify four times? And he heard women wailing and forbade them, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid lamentations."
"735","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Al-Ahzab saying: O Allah, Sender of the Book, Swift in reckoning, Mover of the clouds, defeat the confederates; O Allah, defeat them and shake them."
"736","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, he said: I said to Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) give Khadijah glad tidings of a house in Paradise of hollow pearl, in which there is neither noise nor toil? He said: Yes."
"737","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa say: We performed umrah with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we would shield him while he circumambulated from the children of the people of Makkah lest they harm him. Sufyan said: I think it was in the compensatory umrah. Ismail said: And Ibn Abi Awfa showed us a wound that struck him with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Hunayn."
"738","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Mighwal narrated to us, from Talhah ibn Musarrif, who said: I asked Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) make a bequest? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left nothing concerning which a bequest is made. I said: How did he command people with bequests yet make none himself? He said: He bequeathed the Book of Allah. Talhah said: Al-Huzayl ibn Shurahbil said: Shall Abu Bakr take precedence over the legatee of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? Abu Bakr would have wished to find a covenant from the Messenger of Allah by which to rein his nose [flag: idiom khazama bihi anfahu, i.e. to restrain or control him]."
"739","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Bara ibn Azib say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say at his resting place, or he commanded that it be said at the resting place, or he commanded me to say at my resting place - Sufyan doubted it, not knowing which of them he said: O Allah, to You I have turned my face, to You I have submitted myself, to You I have entrusted my affair, and to You I have laid my back, in hope and fear of You; there is no refuge nor escape from You except to You; I believe in Your Book which You sent down and Your Prophet whom You sent. They said to him: And Your Messenger whom You sent, but he refused except: And Your Prophet."
"740","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to us at Makkah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from al-Bara ibn Azib, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raise his hands when he opened the prayer. Sufyan said: Then he came to Kufah, and I heard him narrate it with the addition: Then he does not repeat it. I thought they had prompted him with it; for at Makkah that day he had a better memory than the day I saw him at Kufah, and they told me that his memory had changed, or his memory had worsened."
"741","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Aban ibn Taghlib - and he was eloquent - narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from al-Bara ibn Azib, who said: None of us would bend down until he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fall prostrate."
"742","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said and Misar ibn Kidam narrated to us that they both heard Adi ibn Thabit narrate from al-Bara, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reciting in Maghrib: By the fig and the olive. Sufyan said: Misar added: I never heard a man with a finer recitation than his."
"743","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us that he heard Abu al-Minhal say: A partner of mine sold dirhams for dirhams at Kufah with an excess between them. I said: I do not consider this lawful. He said: I sold them in the market, and no one objected to me about it. So I went to al-Bara ibn Azib and asked him. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah while our trade was thus, and he said: Whatever is hand to hand, there is no harm in it; and whatever is deferred, there is no good in it. And go to Zayd ibn Arqam, for he was greater in trade than I. So I went to him and mentioned that to him, and he said: Al-Bara spoke the truth. Al-Humaydi said: This is abrogated and is not acted upon [flag: editorial remark by al-Humaydi retained literally]."
"744","In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me, from Abu Said al-Khudri: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw phlegm in the qiblah of the mosque, took a pebble and scraped it off, and forbade a man to spit in front of him or to his right, saying: Let him spit to his left or under his left foot."
"745","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us that he heard Iyad ibn Abdullah ibn Sad ibn Abi Sarh: that he heard Abu Said al-Khudri say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to like these palm stalks, holding them in his hand and entering the mosque with them in his hand. He saw phlegm in the qiblah of the mosque and scraped it off, then turned to the people in anger and said: Would one of you like to be spat upon in his face? Then he said: When a servant stands for prayer, he only faces his Lord, so let him not spit in front of him nor to his right; let him spit to his left or under his left foot. If he is hurried by an impulse while praying, let him spit into his garment and do thus. And Sufyan rubbed with his sleeve."
"746","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi informed me, from Abu Said, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade two transactions and two ways of dress. As for the two transactions: touching and tossing; and as for the two ways of dress: wrapping in a single garment with no opening, and a man sitting with his knees drawn up in a single garment with nothing of it over his private part."
"747","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Damrah ibn Said al-Mazini narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Said al-Khudri say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade prayer after the Asr prayer until the sun sets, and prayer after the morning prayer until the sun rises."
"748","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sasah narrated to us, he said: I heard my father - and he was an orphan in the care of Abu Said - say: Abu Said said to me: O my son, when you are in these deserts, raise your voice with the adhan, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Nothing hears it, neither man nor jinn, neither stone nor tree nor anything, except that it will testify for him on the Day of Resurrection."
"749","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sasah narrated that he heard his father say: I heard Abu Said al-Khudri say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is imminent that the best wealth of a Muslim man will be sheep with which he follows the mountain peaks and the places of rainfall, fleeing with his religion from tribulations."
"750","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Khusayfah narrated to us, he said: I heard Busr ibn Said say: Abu Said al-Khudri narrated to me, he said: I was in a circle in which Ubayy ibn Kab was seated when Abu Musa al-Ashari came to us alarmed, or he said frightened. We said: What is the matter with you? He said: Umar sent for me concerning some need, so I went to him and sought permission three times but was not permitted, so I returned. I said to him that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When one of you seeks permission three times and is not permitted, let him return. Umar said: You shall surely bring proof for what you said, or I shall do such-and-such to you. Ubayy ibn Kab said to me: None shall stand with you except the youngest of the people. Abu Said said: So I was the youngest of the people, and I went to Umar and told him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you seeks permission three times and is not permitted, let him return."
"751","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Yahya ibn Umarah ibn Abi al-Hasan al-Mazini narrated to us, he said: My father informed me that he heard Abu Said al-Khudri say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no charity on less than five dhawd of camels, no charity on less than five awsuq of grain, and no charity on less than five uqiyahs of silver. Sufyan said: Amr ibn Dinar and Yahya ibn Said used to narrate this hadith from Amr ibn Yahya."
"752","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Safwan ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bathing on Friday is obligatory upon every one who has reached puberty."
"753","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yaqub, freedman of al-Huraqah, narrated to me, he said: I heard my father say: I went to Abu Said al-Khudri and asked him: Did you hear anything from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning the lower garment? He said: Yes; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The lower garment of the believer is to the middle of his shins; there is no sin upon him in what is between that and the ankles; what is below the ankles is in the Fire; Allah, Mighty and Majestic, does not look at one who drags his garment in arrogance."
"754","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Suhayl ibn Abi Salih narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn Bashir, from Said al-Asha, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has three daughters, or three sisters, or two daughters, or two sisters, and keeps good company with them, is patient with them, and fears Allah concerning them, shall enter Paradise."
"755","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said and Abu Umayr al-Harith ibn Umayr narrated to us that they both heard from Abu Tuwalah narrating from Nahar al-Abdi, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah will question the servant on the Day of Resurrection until He says: What prevented you, when you saw wrong in the world, from denouncing it? And when Allah prompts His servant with his plea, he will say: O Lord, I hoped in You and feared people."
"756","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us that he heard Iyad ibn Abdullah ibn Sad ibn Abi Sarh al-Amiri say: I heard Abu Said al-Khudri say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said upon the pulpit: What I fear most for you is what Allah, Mighty and Majestic, brings forth of the vegetation of the earth and the splendor of the world. He said: A man stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, can good bring evil? Three times. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell silent until we thought revelation was descending upon him - and when revelation descended upon him, heaviness of breathing and sweat would cover him - and when it was lifted from him he said: Where is the questioner? He said: Here I am, O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I intended nothing but good. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Good brings nothing but good; good brings nothing but good; good brings nothing but good. But the world is green and sweet, and everything the spring grows kills by overeating or nearly does, except the eater of green fodder: it eats until, when its flanks distend, it faces the sun, drops its dung or urinates, then returns and eats, then empties and ruminates. Whoever takes wealth rightfully, it is blessed for him in it; whoever takes wealth without right, it is not blessed for him in it, and he is like one who eats but is not satiated. The upper hand is better than the lower hand. Sufyan said: Al-Amash would often have me repeat this hadith whenever I came to him."
"757","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, he said: Iyad ibn Abdullah ibn Sad ibn Abi Sarh narrated to us, he said: I saw Abu Said al-Khudri come while Marwan ibn al-Hakam was delivering the sermon on Friday. He stood to pray the two rakahs, and the guards came to him to seat him, but he refused to sit until he had prayed the two rakahs. When he finished the prayer we went to him and said to him: O Abu Said, they almost did something to you. Abu Said said: I would not leave them for anything after something I saw from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while a man came as he was delivering the sermon on Friday; he entered the mosque in shabby appearance, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Have you prayed? He said: No. He said: Then pray two rakahs. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) urged the people to give charity, and the people threw garments, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave the man two garments from them. When the next Friday came, the man came while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was delivering the sermon, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Have you prayed two rakahs? He said: No. He said: Then pray two rakahs. Then he urged the people to give charity, and they threw garments, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave the man two garments from them. When the next Friday came, the man came while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was delivering the sermon, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Have you prayed two rakahs? He said: No. He said: Then pray two rakahs. Then he urged the people to give charity, and they threw garments, and the man threw one of his two garments. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shouted at him and said: Take it. So he took it. Then he said: Look at this one: he came that Friday in shabby appearance, so I commanded the people to give charity, they threw garments, and I gave him two garments from them. When this Friday came, I commanded the people to give charity, and he threw one of his two garments. Sufyan said, he says: There is no charity except out of sufficiency, and he has no sufficiency to do without his garment."
"758","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ajlan narrated to us that he heard Iyad ibn Abdullah say: I heard Abu Said al-Khudri say: We would give nothing on the days of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for the charity of breaking the fast except a sa of dates, a sa of barley, or a sa of dried curd."
"759","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah say: Abu Said al-Khudri narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will come upon people a time when a company of people go forth to battle, and it will be said: Is there among you one who accompanied the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? It will be said: Yes, and victory will be granted to them. Then there will come upon people a time when a company of people go forth to battle, and it will be said to them: Is there among you one who accompanied the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? It will be said to them: Yes, and victory will be granted to them. Then there will come upon people a time when a company of people go forth to battle, and it will be said to them: Is there among you one who accompanied one who accompanied the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? It will be said: Yes, and victory will be granted to them."
"760","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, he said: Abu Salih al-Samman informed me, he said: I heard Abu Said al-Khudri narrate that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Dirham for dirham and dinar for dinar, like for like, with no excess between them. I said to Abu Said al-Khudri: But Ibn Abbas sees no harm in it. Abu Said said: I met Ibn Abbas and said to him: Tell me about this that you say: is it something you found in the Book of Allah, or something you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: I neither found it in the Book of Allah nor heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and you know the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) better than I. But Usamah ibn Zayd informed me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Usury is in deferment."
"761","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Damrah ibn Said al-Mazini narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Said al-Khudri narrate from Umar the hadith of exchange from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And Ibn Umar came and asked him about it while I was present. Sufyan said: I retain nothing of it except that it is similar to what people narrate from Abu Said, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), concerning gold for gold, like for like, and silver for silver, like for like [flag: Sufyan states he does not retain the wording beyond this gist]."
"762","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated it to me, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: I stationed a slave girl of mine to sell in the market of Banu Qaynuqa, and a Jewish man came to me and said: O Abu Said, what is this slave girl? I said: A slave girl of mine I am selling. He said: Perhaps you will sell her while there is a lamb of yours in her belly. I said: I used to practice withdrawal from her. He said: That is the lesser burying alive. So I went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, and he said: The Jews lied; and it is no harm upon you not to do so."
"763","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Najih narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Qazah, from Abu Said al-Khudri: that withdrawal was mentioned before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Why would one of you do that? And he did not say: Let none of you do that. No soul is created except that Allah is its Creator."
"764","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Mujalid narrated to us, from Abu al-Waddak Jabr ibn Nawf, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"765","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Zayd ibn Judan narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour shall not rise until two great parties of Muslims fight one another, their claim being one; the nearer of them to the truth is the one that prevails. While they are thus, a renegade faction shall secede from them, passing out of the religion as an arrow passes through the game."
"766","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to us, he said: Qazah informed me, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Mounts are not saddled except to three mosques: the Sacred Mosque, this mosque of mine, and the mosque of Iliya. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No woman should travel more than three days except with a mahram. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade prayer after Asr until the sun sets, and prayer after dawn until the sun rises; and he forbade fasting two days: the day of sacrifice and the day of breaking the fast."
"767","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, he said: Attab ibn Hunayn informed me, he said: I heard Abu Said al-Khudri say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If Allah withheld rain from people for seven years then sent it, a party of them would wake in the morning disbelieving in Him, saying: We were rained upon by such-and-such star, or: We were rained upon by the star of al-Mijdah."
"768","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Zayd ibn Judan narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us after Asr until near sunset, and nothing that shall be until the rising of the Hour remained except that he informed us of it; whoever knew it knew it, and whoever was ignorant of it was ignorant of it. He said: The world is green and sweet, and Allah is making you stewards in it, observing how you act. Verily beware of the world and beware of women. Verily every treacherous one shall have a banner on the Day of Resurrection according to his treachery, and a banner at his back. Verily the best jihad is a word of truth - and Sufyan would sometimes say: A word of justice before an unjust ruler. He said: Then Abu Said wept and said: How much wrong we have seen and not denounced: Verily the children of Adam were created in ranks: among them are those born a believer, living a believer, and dying a believer; among them are those born a disbeliever, living a disbeliever, and dying a disbeliever; among them are those born a believer, living a believer, and dying a disbeliever; among them are those born a disbeliever, living a disbeliever, and dying a believer; among them are the quick to anger and quick to return, so this offsets that; among them are the slow to anger and slow to return, so this offsets that. Verily anger is a coal from the Fire; whoever of you feels it and is standing, let him sit; and if he is seated, let him lie down."
"769","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Asim al-Ahwal narrated to us, from Abu al-Mutawakkil al-Naji, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you comes to his wife, if he wishes to return, let him perform ablution as for prayer."
"770","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Mutarrif narrated to us, from Atiyyah al-Awfi, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How can I enjoy when the holder of the Trumpet has taken the Trumpet, bent his forehead, and inclined his ear, waiting for when he shall be commanded? They said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you command us? He said: Say: Allah suffices us, and He is the best Disposer; upon Allah we rely."
"771","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Mighwal narrated to us, from Atiyyah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of the highest ranks shall surely see the people of Illiyyun as you see the brilliant star on the horizon; and Abu Bakr and Umar are among them, and how excellent."
"772","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Alqamah narrated to us, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Said al-Khudri [flag: Arabic text breaks off here with ellipsis, no matn present in source]."
"773","Sufyan said: And Ibn Jurayj narrated it to us, from Sulayman ibn Abi Muslim al-Ahwal, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) observed itikaf in the middle ten of the month of Ramadan, and we observed itikaf with him. When the morning of the twentieth came, we moved our belongings, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw us and said: Whoever of you was observing itikaf, let him return to his place of itikaf, for I was shown it in the last ten, and I saw myself prostrating in its morning in water and mud. The sky clouded over at the end of that day and it rained; the mosque was of palm branches, and it dripped in the prayer place of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turn from the dawn prayer with traces of water and mud upon his forehead and nose."
"774","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Muhammad ibn Sad ibn Abi Waqqas narrates, saying: Hamzah ibn al-Mughirah ibn Shubah informed me, he said: I heard my father say: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and he said to me: Stay behind, O Mughirah, and proceed, O people. He said: The people proceeded and I stayed behind. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to relieve himself, then came, and I poured for him from a water skin, while he wore a Roman cloak. He went to take out his hand, but the cloak was tight upon him, so he took it out from beneath it. He washed his face and his hands, wiped his head, then wiped over his leather socks. Sufyan said: Ismail said to me: I narrated it to al-Zuhri, and one day he narrated the hadiths of wiping over leather socks; when he finished what he had of the hadith, he turned to me and said: And he narrated to me from Hamzah ibn al-Mughirah, then continued in my hadith until he finished it."
"775","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah, Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, and Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Shabi, from Urwah ibn al-Mughirah ibn Shubah, from his father, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, may one of us wipe over the leather socks? He said: Yes, when he put them on while they were pure."
"776","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to me, he said: Ziyad ibn Ilaqah narrated to me, he said: I heard al-Mughirah ibn Shubah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood until his feet swelled. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, has Allah not forgiven you what preceded of your sin and what followed? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not be a grateful servant?"
"777","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Waki ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, he said: Tumah ibn Amr al-Jafari narrated to us, from Umar ibn Bayan al-Taghlibi, from Urwah ibn al-Mughirah ibn Shubah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sells wine, let him carve up pigs [flag: obscure idiom fal-yushaqqis al-khanazir rendered literally]."
"778","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Mutarrif ibn Tarif and Abd al-Malik ibn Sa'id ibn Abjar both narrated to us, both of whom heard al-Sha'bi say: I heard al-Mughira ibn Shu'ba on the pulpit, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: Musa asked his Lord, mighty and majestic, and said: My Lord, who among the people of Paradise is of the lowest station? He said: A man who comes after the people of Paradise have entered Paradise, and it is said to him: Enter Paradise, though they have already taken their dwellings and received their shares. It is said to him: Would you be pleased for you to have the like of what one of the kings of this world had? He says: Yes, my Lord, I am pleased. He says: It is said to him: Then yours is this, and the like of it, and the like of it, and the like of it, and the like of it. He says: I am pleased, my Lord. He says: It is said to him: Then yours is this, and ten times as much along with it. He says: I am pleased, my Lord. He says: It is said to him: Then yours is, along with this, whatever your soul desires and your eye delights in. Musa said: My Lord, then who among the people of Paradise is of the highest station? He said: That is what I intended, and I shall tell you of them: I planted their honor with My hand and sealed it, so no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and it has never occurred to the heart of a human. He said: And the confirmation of that is in the Book of Allah, mighty and majestic: No soul knows what is hidden for them of comfort for the eyes."
"779","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abdah ibn Abi Lubaba and Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to us, both of whom heard Warrad, the scribe of al-Mughira ibn Shu'ba, say: Mu'awiya ibn Abi Sufyan wrote to al-Mughira: Write to me something you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So al-Mughira wrote to him: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say when he finished his prayer: There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner for Him; to Him belongs sovereignty and to Him belongs praise, and He has power over all things. O Allah, none can withhold what You have given, and none can give what You have withheld, and the wealth of the wealthy avails him nothing against You."
"780","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Najih narrated to us, from Mujahid, from al-Aqqar ibn al-Mughira ibn Shu'ba, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever seeks ruqya or cauterization has not placed his trust in Allah."
"781","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, he said: I heard Qays ibn Abi Hazim say: I heard al-Mughira ibn Shu'ba say: No one asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the Dajjal as I asked him. He said: And what is your asking about him? You will never live to see him."
"782","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani narrated to us, from Abu Qilaba, from Zahdam al-Jarmi, who said: We were with Abu Musa al-Ash'ari when chicken meat was brought, and a man withdrew and did not eat. Abu Musa called him and he said: I saw it eating something filthy. Abu Musa said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eating it."
"783","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Qilaba, from Zahdam, from Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, who said: We came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking him for mounts, and a herd of camels with white humps was brought. We said: O Messenger of Allah, give us mounts. He swore he would not give us mounts, then another herd was brought. We said: O Messenger of Allah, give us mounts, and he gave us mounts. When we turned away we said: What have we done? We caught the Messenger of Allah unawares regarding his oath. So we came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I never swear an oath and then see something better than it except that I do what is better and expiate for my oath."
"784","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: A shaykh from the people of Kufa called Shu'ba, and he was trustworthy, narrated to us, he said: I was with Abu Burda ibn Abi Musa in his house on its roof, and he called his sons and said: O my sons, come so I may narrate to you a hadith I heard from my father, who narrated it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I heard my father say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever frees a slave, Allah, mighty and majestic, frees for every limb of that slave a limb of his from the Fire."
"785","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Salih ibn Hayy narrated to us, he said: A man came to al-Sha'bi while I was with him and said: O Abu Amr, there are people with us in Khurasan who say: When a man frees his slave-girl then marries her, he is like one riding his sacrificial camel. Al-Sha'bi said: Abu Burda ibn Abi Musa narrated to us, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three will be given their reward twice: a man of the People of the Book who was a believer before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sent, then believed in the Prophet, so he has two rewards; a man who had a slave-girl whom he taught and taught well, disciplined and disciplined well, then freed her and married her, so he has two rewards; and a slave who obeys Allah and fulfills the right of his master, so he has two rewards. Take it for nothing; a man would travel for less than it to Medina."
"786","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Burayd ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Burda narrated to us, from his grandfather Abu Burda, from Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The trustworthy treasurer who gives what he is commanded to give, seeking reward, is one of the givers of charity."
"787","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Burayd ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Burda narrated to us, from his grandfather Abu Burda, from Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The example of the righteous companion is like that of the perfume seller; if none of his perfume reaches you, some of its fragrance clings to you. And the example of the evil companion is like that of the blacksmith; if his sparks do not burn you, some of his odor clings to you."
"788","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Burayd ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Burda narrated to us, from his grandfather Abu Burda, from Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Intercede to me and you will be rewarded, and let Allah decree upon the tongue of His Prophet whatever He wills."
"789","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Burayd ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Burda narrated to us, from Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer to the believer is like a building, each part strengthening the other."
"790","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Khusayfa narrated to us, from Busr ibn Sa'id, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When one of you seeks permission three times and is not granted it, let him return."
"791","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, Amr ibn Sa'id al-Thawri narrated to us, from al-A'mash, who said: I heard Sa'id ibn Jubayr say: There is no one more patient with hurt he hears than Allah, mighty and majestic; they ascribe to Him an equal, yet He provides for them and grants them health. Al-A'mash said: It was said to him: From whom did you hear this, O Abu Abd Allah? He said: But I have not lied; Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami narrated to us, from Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"792","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Aswad ibn Qays narrated to us, while he was picking lice in the sun in winter, saying: I heard Jundub al-Bajali say: I attended the Eid with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he learned that some people had slaughtered before the prayer, so he said: Whoever among you slaughtered before the prayer, let him repeat his sacrifice, and whoever has not slaughtered, let him slaughter in the name of Allah."
"793","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Aswad ibn Qays narrated to us, he said: I heard Jundub ibn Abd Allah al-Bajali say: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a cave when his finger was injured, and he said: You are but a finger that has bled, and what you have met is in the path of Allah."
"794","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Aswad ibn Qays narrated to us, he said: Jundub ibn Abd Allah al-Bajali narrated to us, he said: Jibril, peace be upon him, was delayed in bringing revelation to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the polytheists said: Muhammad has been forsaken. Then Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed: By the morning brightness, and by the night when it covers, your Lord has not forsaken you, nor does He hate you."
"795","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Harb, the truthful and trustworthy, narrated to us, he said: I heard Salama ibn Kuhayl say: I never heard anyone who heard from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Jundub al-Bajali. I heard Jundub say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever seeks reputation, Allah will make his bad reputation known, and whoever shows off, Allah will make his showing off known."
"796","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to us, he said: I heard Jundub al-Bajali say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Verily I shall precede you at the Pond. Sufyan said: And something else was mentioned in it."
"797","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, who said: I heard al-Sunabihi al-Ahmasi say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Verily I shall precede you at the Pond, and I shall outnumber the nations through you, so do not fight one another after me. Al-Humaydi narrated to us: Al-Sunabihi is Abu al-A'sar, and Sufyan did not tell us that; we learned it from another source."
"798","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utba informed me that he heard Ibn Abbas say: al-Sa'b ibn Jaththama informed me, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say, when he was asked about the households of the polytheists who are attacked by night so that their women and offspring are struck: They are from them. Sufyan said: Amr had first narrated it to us from al-Zuhri with the wording: They are from their fathers. When al-Zuhri came to us I checked it, and he said nothing but: They are from them."
"799","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah informed me that he heard Ibn Abbas say: al-Sa'b ibn Jaththama informed me, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no reserved pasture except for Allah and His Messenger."
"800","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah informed me that he heard Ibn Abbas say: al-Sa'b ibn Jaththama informed me, he said: I presented to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the meat of a wild donkey while he was at al-Abwa or Waddan, and he returned it to me. When he saw displeasure in my face he said: It is not that we return it to you out of rejection, but we are in ihram. Al-Humaydi said: Sufyan would sometimes combine both together in one hadith and sometimes separate them, and Sufyan would say wild donkey, then later adopted the wording meat of a wild donkey."
"801","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Muslim ibn Yannaq, from Tawus, who said: I saw Ibn Abbas meet Zayd ibn Arqam and begin asking him to recall a hadith: How did you narrate to me from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning the meat of game? Then Zayd ibn Arqam mentioned from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) something like the hadith of al-Sa'b ibn Jaththama."
"802","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Ajlah ibn Abd Allah ibn Hujayya al-Kindi narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Khalil, from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: Ali ibn Abi Talib was brought, while in Yemen, a case of three men who had intercourse with a slave-girl of theirs in one purity period, and she gave birth to a child. Ali said to two of them: Do you willingly give him up to your companion? They said: No. Then he said to another two: Do you willingly give him up to your companion? They said: No. Then he said to another two: Do you willingly give him up to your companion? They said: No. Then Ali said: You are quarrelsome partners; I shall cast lots among you, and whichever of you the lot falls upon, I shall attach the child to him and make him pay two-thirds of the value of the slave-girl to his two companions. When we came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) we mentioned that to him, and he said: I know nothing concerning it except what Ali said."
"803","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu Sahl narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from Ali ibn Dhuray, from Zayd ibn Arqam, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it."
"804","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, he said: Ata ibn Abi Rabah informed me, from Safwan ibn Ya'la, from his father, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reciting on the pulpit: And they will call: O Malik."
"805","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ata, from Safwan ibn Ya'la, from his father, who said: I fought alongside the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the expedition of Tabuk. I carried another on a young camel there, and it was the most reliable of my deeds in my own view. I hired a laborer who fought a man; the man bit his hand and he pulled it from his mouth, knocking out his front tooth. He came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Would he leave it in your mouth for you to chew it as the stallion chews? And he annulled it."
"806","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr narrated to us, from Ata, that a hireling of Ya'la, and he did not raise it with a chain, and Sufyan would sometimes join them together and insert the chain into it, but when he separated them he made the hadith of Ibn Jurayj raised with a chain and made the hadith of Amr disconnected."
"807","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr narrated to us, he said: Ata informed me, he said: Safwan ibn Ya'la informed me, from his father, who said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at al-Ji'rana when a man came to him wearing a cut-up garment, meaning a cloak, and smeared with khaluq perfume. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I have entered ihram for umra while this is upon me. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: What would you do in your hajj? He said: I would wash off this khaluq and remove this cut-up garment. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever you would do in your hajj, do it in your umra."
"808","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ata, from Safwan ibn Ya'la, from his father, who said: I said to Umar ibn al-Khattab: I long to see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when revelation descends upon him. He said: While I was at al-Ji'rana, Umar called me, so I came, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was covered with a garment. Umar uncovered his face for me, and his face was red. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was relieved of it, he said: Where is the questioner? A man had come to him before that, smeared with khaluq and wearing a cut-up garment, saying: I have entered ihram while this is upon me. The questioner said: Here I am. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What would you do in your hajj? He said: I would wash off this khaluq and remove this cut-up garment. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever you would do in your hajj, do it in your umra."
"809","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakra informed me, he said: My father dictated to me a letter to a brother of mine who was a governor, that he should not judge between two disputants while angry. For I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: It is not proper for a judge to judge between two while he is angry."
"810","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Isra'il Abu Musa narrated to us, from al-Hasan, who said: I heard Abu Bakra say: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the pulpit with al-Hasan ibn Ali beside him, turning to the people once and to him once, saying: This son of mine is a leader, and perhaps Allah will reconcile through him between two groups of Muslims."
"811","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Ilaqa narrated to us, he said: I heard Jarir ibn Abd Allah al-Bajali say: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to give sincere counsel to every Muslim. Sufyan said: And he added in it, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqa, from Jarir, that he said: And I am indeed sincere toward you."
"812","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, he said: I heard Qays narrating from Jarir ibn Abd Allah, who said: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to establish prayer, give zakat, and give sincere counsel to every Muslim."
"813","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Abi Hind and Mujalid narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from Jarir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the collector comes to you, let him not leave you except with your consent."
"814","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim al-Nakha'i, from Hammam ibn al-Harith, who said: I saw Jarir ibn Abd Allah performing ablution from the ablution vessel of the mosque from which the common people perform ablution, then wiping over his leather socks. It was said to him: Do you do this? He said: What prevents me, when I have seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiping over his leather socks? Ibrahim said: This hadith used to please the companions of Abd Allah, because the Islam of Jarir came after the revelation of al-Ma'ida."
"815","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Mujalid narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from Jarir, who said: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to hear and obey, establish prayer, give zakat, and give sincere counsel to every Muslim."
"816","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, he said: I heard Qays say: I heard Jarir ibn Abd Allah say: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the night of the fourteenth of the month, and he said: Do you see this moon? You shall see your Lord as you see this moon, without being wronged in seeing Him. So whoever of you is able not to be overcome regarding a prayer before sunrise and before sunset, let him do so."
"817","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, he said: I heard Qays say: I heard Jarir ibn Abd Allah al-Bajali say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never saw me but smiled in my face."
"818","He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There shall come upon you through this door a man from the best of Dhi Yaman, with the trace of an angel upon his face. Then Jarir ibn Abd Allah came through."
"819","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Isma'il narrated to us, he said: I heard Qays say: I heard Jarir ibn Abd Allah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Will you not relieve me of this Khalasa of Yemen? I said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a man who cannot keep firm upon horses. He said: He struck my chest and said: O Allah, make him firm and make him a guide, rightly guided. He said: I went out, Sufyan said, with forty, or he said fifty, riders of my people, and I burned it. Then I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I did not come to you until I left it like a mangy camel, or he said bald. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) then supplicated three times for the horses and men of Ahmas."
"820","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan and Marwan ibn Mu'awiya narrated to us, both said: Isma'il narrated to us, from Qays, from Jarir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah will not show mercy to him."
"821","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr, who said: Mu'awiya ibn Abi Sufyan appointed Jarir ibn Abd Allah over a detachment, and they were struck by severe cold, so Jarir brought them back. Mu'awiya said to him: Why did you bring them back? Jarir said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah will not show mercy to him. Mu'awiya said to him: Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah? He said: Yes."
"822","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Mu'awiya wanted to show the people that he only left him because he had narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so that no one else would dare to return without his permission."
"823","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Asim ibn Bahdala narrated to us, from Shaqiq, from Jarir, who said: Some people wearing patched woolen garments came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him, so he urged the people to give charity, and they gave little, until that was seen in the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then a man of the Ansar came with a piece of gold, or he said raw gold, and threw it down, and the people followed one after another, until that was seen in the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever establishes a good practice and it is acted upon, he shall have a reward like the reward of whoever acts upon it, without diminishing anything from their rewards. And whoever establishes an evil practice and it is acted upon, upon him shall be a burden like the burden of whoever acts upon it, without diminishing anything from their burdens."
"824","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Jarir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a slave flees to the land of the enemy, the protection of Allah, mighty and majestic, is absolved from him."
"825","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: One of our companions narrated to us, from Habib, from al-Mughira, from Jarir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"826","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Thabit ibn Abi Safiyya Abu Hamza, from Zadham, from Jarir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: The lahd grave is for us, and the shaqq is for others."
"827","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Maysara narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn al-Sharid informed me, from his father, who said: I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he said to me: Do you have any of the poetry of Umayya ibn Abi al-Salt with you? I said: Yes. He said: Recite. So I recited a verse to him, then he said: Recite, and I recited a verse to him, and he kept saying: Recite, until I had recited a hundred verses to him."
"828","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Maysara narrated to us, from Amr ibn al-Sharid, or Ya'qub ibn Asim, as Sufyan would doubt concerning it, from al-Sharid, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man who had let his lower garment trail, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Raise your lower garment. The man said: O Messenger of Allah, I am bow-legged and my knees knock together. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Raise your lower garment, for all of Allah's creation is good. That man was never seen thereafter except with his lower garment to the middle of his shins."
"829","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utba informed me, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, Abu Hurayra, and Shibl, who said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a man stood up to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I adjure you by Allah, judge between us only by the Book of Allah. His opponent stood, and he was more understanding than him, and said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, judge between us by the Book of Allah, and permit me to speak. He said: Speak. He said: My son was a laborer for this man, and he committed adultery with his wife. I was told that my son deserved stoning, so I ransomed him with a hundred sheep and a servant. Then I asked men of knowledge, and they told me that upon my son is a hundred lashes and exile for a year, and upon this man's wife is stoning. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, I shall judge between you by the Book of Allah: the hundred sheep and the servant are to be returned to you; upon your son is a hundred lashes and exile for a year; and go, O Unays, to this man's wife, and if she confesses, stone her. He said: He went to her in the morning and she confessed, so he stoned her. Sufyan said: And Unays is a man of Aslam."
"830","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utba narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Khalid, Abu Hurayra, and Shibl, who said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he was asked about a slave-girl who commits adultery before being married. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the slave-girl of one of you commits adultery, flog her; if she repeats, flog her; if she repeats, flog her. He said regarding the third or fourth time: Then sell her, even for a rope of hair, meaning a rope made of hair."
"831","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Salih ibn Kaysan narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utba informed me, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, who said: People were rained upon in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at night, and when morning came the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Have you not heard what your Lord said last night? He said: No blessing of Mine upon My servants comes but a group of them wake up disbelieving in it, saying: We were rained upon by such-and-such a star. As for whoever believes in Me and praises Me for My watering, that is the one who believes in Me and disbelieves in the star. And as for whoever says: We were rained upon by such-and-such a star, that is the one who believes in the star and disbelieves in Me, or disbelieves in My blessing. Sufyan said: Ma'mar had first narrated it to us from Salih, then we heard it from Salih himself."
"832","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Salih ibn Kaysan narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utba, Sufyan said: I do not know whether it was Zayd ibn Khalid or not, he said: A man reviled a rooster in the presence of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not revile the rooster, for it calls to prayer."
"833","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from Abu Amra, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Khaybar when a man of Ashja' died, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not pray over him, saying: Pray over your companion. They looked into his belongings and found in them beads of Jewish beads not worth two dirhams."
"834","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: I heard Yazid, the freed slave of al-Munba'ith, say: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him about lost property. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Recognize its container and its wrapping, then announce it for a year; if it is claimed, return it, otherwise mix it with your wealth. He said: And he asked him about stray sheep, and he said: It is for you, or for your brother, or for the wolf. And he asked him about stray camels, and he became angry until his cheeks reddened, and said: What have you to do with it? It has its water-skin and its sandals; it comes to water and eats trees until its owner comes to it. Sufyan said: It reached me that Rabi'a ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman raised it with a chain from Zayd ibn Khalid, so I came to him and said to him: Is the hadith you narrate from Yazid, the freed slave of al-Munba'ith, concerning lost property and stray camels and sheep, from Zayd ibn Khalid, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes. And I used to dislike it as mere opinion, so for that reason I did not ask him about it, and had he not raised it with a chain I would not have asked him about its chain."
"835","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Salim Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, from Busr ibn Sa'id, who said: Abu al-Juhaym sent me to ask Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani: What did you hear concerning one who passes in front of a praying person? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: For one of you to wait forty is better for him than to pass in front of a praying person. He does not know whether he said forty years, forty months, forty days, or forty hours."
"836","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever equips a warrior or takes his place among his family has himself fought."
"837","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Harun ibn Ri'ab, who used to conceal asceticism, narrated to us, he said: I heard Kinana ibn Nu'aym narrating from Qabisa ibn al-Mukhariq, who said: I took upon myself a blood-money burden, so I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him. He said: We shall pay it or discharge it on your behalf when the charity camels come. Then he said: Begging is forbidden except in three cases: a man who takes upon himself a blood-money burden, for whom begging is lawful until he discharges it, then he refrains; a man struck by poverty and need, until three men of understanding from his people testify or speak that he is in poverty and need, for whom begging is lawful until he attains sufficiency of livelihood or support of livelihood, then he refrains; and a man struck by a calamity that destroys his wealth, for whom begging is lawful until he attains sufficiency of livelihood or support of livelihood, then he refrains. Whatever is besides that is unlawful gain."
"838","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Nawfal ibn Musahiq narrated to us, that he heard a man of Muzayna called Ibn Isam narrating from his father, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dispatched a detachment he would say: When you see a mosque or hear a caller to prayer, do not kill anyone. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent us in a detachment and commanded us with that. We set out toward Tihama and caught up with a man driving women in litters. We said to him: Submit. He said: What is Islam? We told him of it, and he did not know it. He said: What if I do not do so, what will you do? He said: We said: We shall kill you. He said: Will you grant me respite until I catch up with the litters? We said: Yes, and we shall catch up with you. He said: He caught up with the litters and said: Submit, Hunaysh, before life runs out. The other woman said: I submit ten and seven, odd [or eight in succession], then he said: journey by night. He said: Then he returned to us and said: Do as you will. So we brought him forward and struck his neck, and the other woman, a dark pure-bred woman, came down from her litter and crouched over him until she died."
"839","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulayka, from Abd Allah ibn al-Sa'ib: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led the people in the dawn prayer on the day of the Conquest, reciting Surat al-Mu'minin. When he reached the mention of Isa and his mother, a cough or choking seized him, so he bowed."
"840","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ata ibn al-Sa'ib narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Hafs, from Ya'la ibn Murra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw me while I was smeared with perfume, and said to me: O Ya'la, do you have a wife? I said: No. He said: Wash it off and do not repeat, then wash it off and do not repeat. Ya'la said: I washed it off and shall not repeat, then washed it off and shall not repeat, then washed it off and shall not repeat."
"841","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Asim al-Ahwal narrated to us, from Hafsa bint Sirin, from al-Rabab, from her uncle Salman ibn Amir al-Dabbi, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: With the boy is his aqiqa, so shed blood on his behalf and remove harm from him."
"842","He said: And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When one of you breaks his fast, let him break it with dates, for it is blessing; if there are none, then with water, for it is purifying."
"843","And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Charity to a poor person is charity, and it is to a needy relative two things: charity and kinship."
"844","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ziyad ibn Ilaqa narrated to me, he said: I heard Usama ibn Sharik al-Amiri say: I witnessed the Bedouins asking the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Is there any sin upon us in such-and-such, in such-and-such? He said: O servants of Allah, Allah has removed hardship, except for one who backbites something of his brother's honor; that is the one who is in hardship and ruined. They said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we seek treatment? He said: Seek treatment, O servants of Allah, for Allah has not sent down a disease but He has sent down for it a cure, except old age. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the best thing a Muslim servant is given? He said: Good character."
"845","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ziyad ibn Ilaqa narrated to me, he said: I heard my uncle Qutba ibn Malik say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reciting in the dawn prayer: And tall palm trees."
"846","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu al-Tufayl, Amir ibn Wathila, say: I heard Abu Sariha, Hudhayfa ibn Asid al-Ghifari, say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The angel enters upon the sperm-drop after it settles in the womb, after forty, or he said forty-five, nights, and says: My Lord, wretched or blessed? Male or female? So Allah speaks, and both are written. Then his deed, his provision, his term, his trace, and his calamity are written. Then the scroll is folded, and nothing is added to it nor diminished from it. And Sufyan would sometimes say: until the Day of Resurrection, and sometimes not say it."
"847","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Furat al-Qazzaz narrated to us, that he heard Abu al-Tufayl narrating that he heard Abu Sariha al-Ghifari say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked upon us from an upper room of his while we were mentioning the Hour, and said: What were you mentioning? We said: The Hour. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It shall not come until there are ten in it: the Dajjal, the Smoke, the Beast, the rising of the sun from its west, the descent of Isa son of Maryam, Gog and Magog, three eclipses: an eclipse in the east, an eclipse in the west, and an eclipse in the Arabian Peninsula, and the last of that a fire emerging from Aden, or he said from the depths of Aden, driving people to their gathering place."
"848","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Tha'laba informed me that he heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jariya say: I heard my uncle Mujammi' ibn Jariya say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned the Dajjal, say: By the One in whose hand is my soul, the son of Maryam shall surely kill him at the gate of Ludd."
"849","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Qilaba narrating from his uncle, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: Banu Uqayl were allies of Thaqif in the pre-Islamic age, and Thaqif had taken captive two men of the Muslims. Then the Muslims took captive a man of Uqayl with a she-camel of his, and he had a she-camel that had outstripped the pilgrims in the pre-Islamic age so many times; and when a she-camel outstripped the pilgrims in the pre-Islamic age, it was not kept from pasturing where it grazed nor from a trough where it drank. He said: He was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Muhammad, for what did you seize me and seize the forerunner of the pilgrims? He said: For the crime of your allies, Thaqif. He said: And he was detained where the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pass by him. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by him thereafter and he said: O Muhammad, I am a Muslim. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had you said it while you controlled your affair, you would have attained complete success. He said: Then he passed by him another time and he said: O Muhammad, I am hungry, feed me, and thirsty, give me drink. He said: That is your need. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decided, and ransomed with him the two men whom Thaqif had taken captive, keeping the she-camel for himself. Then an enemy raided Medina and took grazing livestock of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), seizing the she-camel among them. He said: And they had with them a Muslim woman they had taken captive, and they would bring the livestock home in the evening. One night the woman came to the livestock and kept coming to no camel but it bellowed, until she reached it, and it did not bellow. So she mounted it and escaped, arriving at Medina. The people said: al-Adba, al-Adba. He said: The woman said: I vowed that if Allah saved me upon it, I would slaughter it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Evil is what you have rewarded it with; there is no fulfillment of a vow in disobedience to Allah, nor in what the son of Adam does not own."
"850","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Four or five narrated to us, among them Ali ibn Zayd ibn Jud'an, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn: that a man freed six slaves of his at his death, having no wealth besides them. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cast lots among them, freeing two and enslaving four, and said: Had I reached him I would not have prayed over him."
"851","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jud'an narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Hasan say: Imran ibn Husayn narrated to us, he said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on one of his journeys when there descended upon him: O people, fear your Lord; indeed the convulsion of the Hour is a great thing. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you know what day that is? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: That is a day when Allah shall say to Adam: O Adam, stand and send forth the delegation of the Fire. He shall say: My Lord, what is the delegation of the Fire? He shall say: From every thousand, nine hundred and ninety-nine to the Fire, and one to Paradise. He said: The people began to weep. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There was never any Islam but ignorance preceded it; the number shall be taken from the ignorance, and if it does not suffice it shall be completed from the hypocrites. And your example among the nations is but like the white mark on the foreleg of a beast or the mole on the side of a camel. Then he said: I hope that you shall be a quarter of the people of Paradise. They exclaimed Allah is Most Great. Then he said: I hope that you shall be a third of the people of Paradise. They exclaimed Allah is Most Great. Then he said: I hope that you shall be half of the people of Paradise, and they exclaimed Allah is Most Great. Sufyan said: My memory ends at the half, and I know only that he said: I hope that you shall be two-thirds of the people of Paradise, or someone else said it."
"852","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jud'an narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As for me, I do not eat reclining; yet he ate food and walked in the markets, meaning the Dajjal."
"853","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jud'an narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn: that Umar ibn al-Khattab adjured the people: Who heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decree anything concerning the grandfather? A man stood and said: I testify that he gave him a third. He said: Along with whom? He said: I do not know. He said: You do not know."
"854","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, and another said: from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn: And another stood to him and said: I testify that he gave him a sixth. He said: Along with whom? He said: I do not know. He said: You do not know."
"855","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Qatada, from Zurara ibn Awfa, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the noon prayer, and when he finished he said: Did any of you recite: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High? A man said: Yes, I did. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I thought that one of you was contending with me for it."
"856","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Husayn narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no ruqya except for the evil eye or a sting."
"857","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Suhayl ibn Abi Salih narrated to us, he said: Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi, a friend of my father from the people of Syria, informed me, from Tamim al-Dari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Religion is sincere counsel, religion is sincere counsel, religion is sincere counsel. They said: To whom, O Messenger of Allah? He said: To Allah, to His Book, to His Prophet, to the leaders of the Muslims and their common folk. Sufyan said: Amr ibn Dinar had first narrated it to us from al-Qa'qa' ibn Hakim, from Abu Salih. When I met Suhayl I said: If only I asked him, perhaps he would narrate it to me from his father, so that I and Amr would be equal in it. So I asked him, and Suhayl said: I heard it from the one from whom my father heard it; Ata ibn Yazid informed me."
"858","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Safwan ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from a woman called Unaysa, from Umm Sa'id, daughter of Murra al-Fihri, from her father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I and the guardian of an orphan, for himself or for another, shall be in Paradise like these two. And Sufyan pointed with his two fingers."
"859","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Umayya narrated to us, he said: It was established for me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I and the guardian of an orphan, for himself or for another, shall be in Paradise, when he is God-fearing, like these two. And al-Humaydi pointed with his finger."
"860","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri and Hisham ibn Urwa narrated to us, both said: Urwa informed us that he heard Abu Humayd al-Sa'idi say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) employed a man of al-Azd called Ibn al-Lutbiyya over charity. When he came he said: This is your wealth, and this was gifted to me. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood upon the pulpit, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: What is the matter with a worker whom we send upon one of our tasks, who says: This is your wealth, and this is what was gifted to me? Why did he not sit in the house of his father or the house of his mother and see whether a gift would come to him or not? Then he said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, none of you takes anything from it but he shall come on the Day of Resurrection carrying it upon his neck, whether a camel with its grumbling, a cow with its lowing, or a sheep bleating. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his hands until we saw the whiteness of his armpits, then said: O Allah, have I conveyed? O Allah, have I conveyed? Sufyan said: And Hisham added in it: Abu Humayd said: My eye saw and my ear heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and ask Zayd ibn Thabit, for he was present with me."
"861","Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Zayd al-Mu'addib recited to us, while I listened, in the year four hundred and twenty-seven, and he acknowledged it. He said: Abu Ali Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Sawwaf narrated to us, recited to him while I listened. He said: Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Shabib ibn Gharqada narrated to us, he said: I heard Urwa ibn Abi al-Ja'd al-Bariqi say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Horses have good tied in their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection."
"862","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Mujalid narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from Urwa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it, adding in it: Reward and spoils."
"863","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Shabib ibn Gharqada narrated to us, that he heard the tribe narrating from Urwa ibn Abi al-Ja'd al-Bariqi: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave him a dinar to buy a sacrificial animal for him. Urwa said: I bought for him two sheep with it, then sold one of them for a dinar, and brought him a dinar and a sheep. He said: He supplicated for me for blessing in trade. He said: Had I bought dust I would have profited in it. Sufyan said: And al-Hasan ibn Umara, I heard him narrating it, said in it: I heard Shabib say: I heard Urwa. When I asked Shabib about it he said: I did not hear it from Urwa; the tribe narrated it to me from Urwa."
"864","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf narrated to us, he said: I heard Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz asking al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid and his companions: What did you hear concerning staying in Mecca? Al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid said: al-Ala ibn al-Hadrami informed me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The stay of the emigrant in Mecca after completing his rites is three days."
"865","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: A shaykh of Banu Ghifar called al-Haytham ibn Abi al-As'ad narrated to us, from his father: that Abu Dharr would stay with them during umra, remaining three days, then departing."
"866","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: al-Rabi' ibn Sabra informed me, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade temporary marriage in the year of the Conquest."
"867","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from al-Rabi' ibn Sabra al-Juhani, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had permitted us temporary marriage. When we arrived at Mecca, I and a cousin of mine went out to a young girl; I had a cloak and my cousin had a cloak better than mine, though I was younger than my cousin. She kept looking and said: A cloak like a cloak. And she chose me, so I gave her my cloak. Then I stayed with her as long as Allah willed. Then I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and found him standing between the Door and Zamzam. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We had permitted you this temporary marriage; whoever has any of these women with him, let him release her, for Allah has forbidden it until the Day of Resurrection, and do not take back anything of what you gave them."
"868","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Sinan ibn Abi Sinan, from Abu Waqid al-Laythi: that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out to Hunayn, he passed by a tree called Dhat Atwat, upon which the polytheists hung their weapons. They said: O Messenger of Allah, make for us a Dhat Atwat as they have a Dhat Atwat. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is Most Great; this is as the Children of Israel said: Make for us a god as they have gods. You shall surely follow the ways of those before you."
"869","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Damra ibn Sa'id al-Mazini narrated to us, he said: I heard Ubayd Allah ibn Utba say: Umar ibn al-Khattab went out on a day of Eid and asked Abu Waqid al-Laythi: With what did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite on this day? Abu Waqid said: With Qaf, and: The Hour has drawn near."
"870","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani narrated to us, from Abu Qilaba, from Thabit ibn al-Dahhak, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever kills himself with something in this world shall be punished with it on the Day of Resurrection."
"871","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi, from one who narrated to him, from Uqba ibn Amir, who said: I descended with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from a mountain pass, and he said to me: Say, O Uqba. I said: What shall I say, O Messenger of Allah? And we separated. I said: O Allah, return it to me from Your Prophet. Then we met and he said to me: Say, O Uqba. I said: What shall I say, O Messenger of Allah? Then we separated. I said: O Allah, return it to me from Your Prophet. Then we met and he said to me: Say, O Uqba. I said: What shall I say, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Say: He is Allah, the One, and: Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of the daybreak, and: Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of mankind. No seeker of refuge ever sought refuge, nor seeker of protection ever sought protection, with the like of them."
"872","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Humayd al-A'raj narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from a man of his people called Mu'adh, or Ibn Mu'adh: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) settled people at Mina in their dwellings, settling the Emigrants and settling the Ansar in their quarter. He said: And he taught the people their rites. He said: And Allah opened our hearing, for we would hear while in our lodgings. Among what he taught us was that he said: When you stone the Jamra, stone it with pebbles like those of khadhf."
"873","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, from Khallad ibn al-Sa'ib, from his father al-Sa'ib ibn Khallad, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril, peace be upon him, came to me and said: Command your companions to raise their voices with ihlal, or he said with talbiya. Sufyan said: Ibn Jurayj had concealed a hadith from me. When Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr came to us I did not tell him of it. When he left for Medina I narrated it to him, and he said to me: O Awf, you hide hadiths from us, and when their people have gone you tell us of them; I shall not narrate it from you. Do you want me to narrate it from you? And he wrote to Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr, and Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr wrote it to him. And Ibn Jurayj would narrate it: Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr wrote to me."
"874","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, from his father, from Abu al-Baddah, from his father: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted the shepherds to stone one day and leave one day."
"875","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, he said: I heard Qays ibn Abi Hazim say: I heard al-Mustawrid, brother of Banu Fihr, say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: This world compared to the Hereafter is but as one of you placing his finger in the sea, then looking at what it returns with. Sufyan said: Ibn Abi Khalid would say in it: I heard al-Mustawrid, brother of Banu Fihr, making a grammatical error in it, so I said: Brother of Banu Fihr, in the accusative."
"876","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Mansur ibn al-Mu'tamir narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Salama ibn Qays al-Ashja'i, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you perform ablution, rinse your nose, and when you clean with stones, use an odd number."
"877","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Salim Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, he said: Zur'a ibn Muslim ibn Jarhad narrated to me, from his grandfather Jarhad, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by me while I was in the mosque wearing a cloak with my thigh uncovered. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Cover your thigh, O Jarhad, for the thigh is nakedness."
"878","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, he said: The family of Jarhad narrated to me, from Jarhad, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"879","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, he said: I said to Jabir ibn Zayd: They claim that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the meat of domestic donkeys. He said: al-Hakam ibn Amr al-Ghifari used to say that among us, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); but the Sea, meaning Ibn Abbas, refused that, reciting: Say: I do not find in what has been revealed to me anything forbidden, to the end of the verse."
"880","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Hakim ibn Jabir, from his father, who said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and saw with him pumpkin. I said: What is this, O Messenger of Allah? He said: We increase the food of our household with it."
"881","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to us, he said: I heard Umara ibn Ruwayba al-Thaqafi say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No one who prayed before sunrise and before sunset shall ever enter the Fire."
"882","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Umara ibn Ruwayba, who said: A man of the people of Basra came to my father and said: Did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No one who prayed before sunrise and before sunset shall ever enter the Fire? My father said: Yes. The Basran said, while he testifies: He indeed heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"883","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Umayya narrated to us, from Muzahim ibn Abi Muzahim, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd Allah ibn Khalid ibn Asid, from Muharrish al-Ka'bi, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed umra from al-Ji'rana by night, and I looked at his back as though it were an ingot of silver, and he entered the morning there as one spending the night. Al-Humaydi said: Sufyan would say in it: Muharrish al-Ka'bi, and if anyone asked him he would say: Muharrish, or Mukharrish, or Mikhrash, sometimes saying this and that, and he always hesitated over the name. Al-Humaydi said: And he is Mukharrish."
"884","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Zuhri say: Safwan ibn Abd Allah ibn Safwan informed me, from Umm al-Darda, from Ka'b ibn Asim al-Ash'ari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fasting while traveling is not righteousness."
"885","Sufyan said: And it was mentioned to me that al-Zuhri would say in it, though I did not hear it myself: Fasting while traveling is not righteousness, in the dialect of Himyar."
"886","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwa narrated to us, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from Sufyan ibn Abi Zuhayr, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Yemen shall be opened, and some people shall come urging their camels on, carrying their families and those who obey them, while Medina is better for them, had they known. Then Iraq shall be opened, and some people shall come urging their camels on, carrying their families and those who obey them, while Medina is better for them, had they known. Then Syria shall be opened, and some people shall come urging their camels on, carrying their families and those who obey them, while Medina is better for them, had they known."
"887","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Sa'id ibn Abjar narrated to us, from Iyad ibn Laqit, from Abu Rimtha al-Sulami, who said: I entered with my father upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and my father saw what was on his back and said: Let me treat what is on your back, for I am a physician. He said: You are a companion, and Allah is the Physician. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to my father: Who is this with you? He said: My son; I testify to him for you. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Verily, you shall not be held for his crime, nor shall he be held for yours. And he mentioned that he saw upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the stain of henna."
"888","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Asim al-Ahwal narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Sarjis, who said: I saw what was on the back of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) like a fist. Sufyan said: Like a large cupping mark."
"889","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Sa'd ibn Sa'id ibn Qays al-Ansari narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith al-Taymi, from Qays, the grandfather of Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw me praying two rak'ahs after the morning prayer and said: What are these two rak'ahs, O Qays? I said: O Messenger of Allah, I had not prayed the two rak'ahs of Fajr, so these are those two rak'ahs. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained silent. Sufyan said: 'Ata ibn Abi Rabah used to narrate this hadith from Sa'd ibn Sa'id."
"890","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi al-Haytham al-Kufi narrated to us, saying: I heard Yusuf ibn Abd Allah ibn Salam saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named me Yusuf."
"891","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to us, that he heard Yusuf ibn Abd Allah ibn Salam saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a man and a woman from the Ansar: Perform 'umrah in the month of Ramadan, for an 'umrah in it for you two is like a Hajj."
"892","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Yazid ibn Yazid ibn Jabir al-Azdi narrated to us, from Makhul, from Ziyad ibn Jariyah, from Habib ibn Maslamah al-Fihri, who said: I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granting a third as additional spoils at the outset of the expedition."
"893","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Hisham ibn 'Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Arqam al-Zuhri: that he went out to Makkah accompanied by some people and he used to lead them in prayer. One day he called the iqamah for prayer, put a man forward to lead, and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the prayer is called and one of you feels the need to relieve himself, let him begin with relieving himself."
"894","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: 'Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from the son of Ka'b ibn Malik, from his father: that when death approached him, Umm Mubashshir said to him: Convey greetings to Mubashshir. Ka'b said to her: O Umm Mubashshir, is this what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said? She said: I do not know; I have become weak, so I seek Allah's forgiveness. Then Ka'b said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The soul of the believer is a green bird that feeds upon the fruits of Paradise."
"895","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: al-Zuhri said: The son of Ka'b ibn Malik informed me, from his uncle: that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent so-and-so - al-Zuhri named him - against Ibn Abi al-Huqayq, he forbade him from killing women and children."
"896","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: I heard al-Zuhri saying: Abu Idris al-Khawlani informed me, from Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade eating every predator that has fangs. Al-Zuhri said: I did not hear this hadith until I came to Sham."
"897","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: al-Zuhri narrated to us, saying: 'Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn 'Umar ibn al-Khattab informed me, from Iyas ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Dhubab, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not strike the female servants of Allah. He said: Then 'Umar came and said: O Messenger of Allah, women have become emboldened against their husbands since you forbade striking them. So he permitted them to strike, and they struck. Then many women gathered around the family of Muhammad complaining, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Tonight seventy women have gathered around the family of Muhammad, each of them complaining about her husband, and you will not find those men to be the best among you."
"898","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Hisham ibn 'Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from al-Hajjaj al-Aslami, from his father, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what removes from me the blame of suckling? He said: A compensation of a slave or a female slave."
"899","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: al-Zuhri narrated to us, saying: Haram ibn Sa'd informed me - Sufyan said: this is the one about whom there is no doubt - and I think he mentioned it from his father: that Muhayyisah asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the earnings of a cupper of his, and he forbade him from it. He kept speaking to him until he said to him: Feed it to your water-carrying camel or feed it to your slaves."
"900","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Ziyad ibn Sa'd and Muhammad ibn 'Ajlan narrated to us, that they both heard 'Amir ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr narrating from his father: that he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicating in prayer in this manner. And al-Humaydi clenched his four fingers and pointed with the index finger. Abu 'Ali - meaning Bishr ibn Musa - said: Abu Bakr is the one who described it to us. Al-Humaydi said: And Sufyan said: Ziyad ibn Sa'd had narrated to me four hadiths heard by Ibn al-Zubayr from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I narrated them but forgot them except this one. Then Ziyad said to me: They are only four."
"901","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Hisham ibn 'Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Najiyah al-Khuza'i, the keeper of the sacrificial camels of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what should I do with the sacrificial camels that break down on the way? He said: Slaughter it, then dip its sandal in its blood, then strike its side with it, then leave it for the people."
"902","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: 'Asim ibn Bahdalah narrated to us, telling us that Zirr ibn Hubaysh said: I came to Safwan ibn 'Assal al-Muradi and he said to me: What has brought you? I said: Seeking knowledge. He said: The angels lower their wings for the seeker of knowledge, pleased with what he seeks. I said: Something has troubled my mind about wiping over the leather socks after relieving oneself, and you were a man from the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I have come to ask you: Did you hear anything about that from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command us, when we were traveling, not to remove our leather socks for three days and their nights except from major impurity, but for relieving oneself, urine, and sleep we would wipe. I said: Did you hear him mention anything about love? He said: Yes, while we were with him on one of his journeys, a Bedouin called out to him in a loud voice: O Muhammad. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) answered him in a similar tone: Here I am. We said to him: Lower your voice, for you have been forbidden from this. He said: No, by Allah, I will not lower my voice. Then he said: O Messenger of Allah, a man loves a people but has not yet joined them? He said: A man is with those whom he loves. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept narrating to us until he said: There is, toward the west, a gate whose breadth is a journey of forty or seventy years, which Allah opened for repentance on the day He created the heavens and the earth, and He will not close it until the sun rises from it."
"903","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hasanah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) urinated while sitting, screened by a shield, and they said: He urinates as a woman urinates. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of the Children of Israel was struck by urine, he would cut it off with scissors, and their companion forbade them from that, and now he is being punished in his grave."
"904","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Za'ra' - 'Amr ibn 'Amr - narrated to us, from his uncle Abu al-Ahwas - 'Awf ibn Malik al-Jushami - from his father, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he looked me up and down and then said: Are you a master of camels or a master of sheep? And the master of camels could be distinguished from the master of sheep by his appearance. I said: Allah has given me of each in abundance. He said: Do you not produce them with sound eyes and ears, then you cut this one and say it is dedicated to the idols, and you slit this one and say it is Bahirah? The hand of Allah is mightier and His knife sharper; if He wished to bring them to you without slit ears, He would do so. Then I said: O Messenger of Allah, to what do you call? He said: To nothing but Allah and kinship. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what have you been sent with? He said: A message from my Lord came to me and I felt constrained by it, fearing my people would disbelieve me, and it was said to me: You shall surely do it. I said: O Messenger of Allah, my cousin comes to me and I swear not to give him nor to uphold ties with him. He said: Expiate for your oath. He said: Then he said: Tell me, if you had two slaves, one who neither betrays you, nor conceals a report from you, nor lies to you, and the other who lies to you, conceals from you, and betrays you, which of them is more beloved to you? I said: The one who neither lies to me, nor betrays me, nor conceals from me. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: So likewise are you in the sight of your Lord."
"905","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, who said: I was with Ziyad ibn Abi al-Ja'd in al-Raqqah, and Ziyad ibn Abi al-Ja'd took my hand and stood me before a man in al-Raqqah and said: This man claims that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man praying alone behind the row and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to repeat the prayer. And his name is Wabisah ibn Ma'bad."
"906","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: 'Asim ibn Kulayb al-Jarmi narrated to us, saying: I heard my father saying: I heard Wa'il ibn Hujr al-Hadrami saying: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raise his hands when he began the prayer, when he bowed, and after he raised his head from bowing. And I saw him, when he sat in prayer, lay his left foot flat, erect his right foot, place his left hand on his left thigh spreading it, place his right hand on his right thigh, clench two fingers, form a ring, and supplicate in this manner. And al-Humaydi raised the index finger. Wa'il said: Then I came to them in winter and saw them raising their hands inside their cloaks."
"907","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Mis'ar narrated to us, from Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il, from his father, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a bucket of Zamzam water. He drank, then performed ablution and rinsed his mouth, then spat it into the bucket as musk - or he said, sweeter than musk - and he blew his nose outside the bucket."
"908","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, who said: A relative of Abd Allah ibn Mughaffal threw pebbles in his presence, so he forbade him from it and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade it and said: It neither hunts game nor harms an enemy, but it gouges out the eye and breaks the tooth. Then he returned and threw pebbles again, so Ibn Mughaffal said to him: I narrate to you from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he forbade it, yet you return to it? I will never speak to you again."
"909","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Malik ibn 'Umayr narrated to us, saying: I heard 'Atiyyah al-Qurazi saying: On the day Sa'd ibn Mu'adh gave judgment concerning Banu Qurayzah, I was a boy. They looked at my waist-wrapper and did not find that I had reached puberty, so here I am among you."
"910","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Najih narrated to us, from Mujahid, who said: I heard a man in the mosque of Kufah saying: On the day Sa'd ibn Mu'adh gave judgment concerning Banu Qurayzah, I was a boy and they doubted about me. They looked at me and did not find that the razor had been used upon me, so I was spared."
"911","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, saying: I walked with Abu Juhayfah to Friday prayer and said to him: Did you see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes, and al-Hasan ibn 'Ali resembled him."
"912","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah and Mis'ar narrated to us, from 'Ali ibn al-Aqmar, from Abu Juhayfah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I do not eat reclining."
"913","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: I heard Malik ibn Mighwal saying: I heard 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah narrating from his father, who said: Bilal came out with the leftover ablution water of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: The people rushed toward it, and I got some of it without sparing effort. He said: And Bilal set up a short spear, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed toward it, while a dog, a woman, and a donkey would pass in front of him."
"914","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, saying: I heard Qays saying: Dukayn ibn Sa'id al-Muzani narrated to me, saying: We came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with four hundred riders asking him for food. He said: O 'Umar, go and feed them and give them. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I have nothing but a few sa's of dates that would not suffice my family through the summer. Then Abu Bakr said: Listen and obey. So 'Umar said: Hearing and obeying. He said: Then 'Umar went until he came to an upper room of his, took out a key from his waist-wrapper, and opened it. He said to the people: Enter. They entered, and I was the last of the people to enter. I took, then I turned and behold, there remained as much as a young camel of dates."
"915","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Isma'il narrated to us, saying: I heard Qays saying: 'Adi ibn 'Amirah al-Kindi narrated to me, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: O people, whomever we appoint among you over a task, let him bring its little and its much. Whoever conceals from us a thread or a needle, and anything beyond that, it is misappropriation which he will bring on the Day of Resurrection. Then a short black man from the Ansar stood up to him - as if I am looking at him now - and said: O Messenger of Allah, take back your task from me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And what is that? He said: What you just said. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And I say now: whomever we appoint among you over a task, let him bring its little and its much. What he is given of it, he may take, and what he is forbidden, he must refrain from."
"916","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Ibn Tawus narrated to us, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appointed 'Ubadah ibn al-Samit over charity, then said to him: Beware, O Abu al-Walid, lest you come on the Day of Resurrection carrying a camel on your neck that bellows, or a cow that lows, or a sheep that bleats. He said: O Messenger of Allah, is that really so? He said: Yes. 'Ubadah said: By the One Who sent you with the truth, I will never work over even two persons again."
"917","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Mis'ar narrated to us, from Ibn al-Qibtiyyah, from Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: We used to pray with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when one of us gave salam, he would gesture with his hand to his right and his left like this: Peace be upon you, peace be upon you. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is the matter with you that you gesture with your hands as if they are the tails of restive horses? Is it not enough for one of you - or rather, it suffices one of you - to place his hand on his thigh, then greet his brother to his right and to his left: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah."
"918","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Azhar, who said: Khalid ibn al-Walid was wounded on the day of Hunayn, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by me while I was a boy, saying: Who will guide me to the baggage of Khalid ibn al-Walid? So I went out running ahead of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: Who will guide to the baggage of Khalid ibn al-Walid? Until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to him while he was leaning against a saddle, wounded. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat beside him and supplicated for him. He said: And I think it includes: and he blew upon him."
"919","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: al-Zuhri narrated to me several hadiths about what fire has touched - some of them saying one performs ablution because of it, and some saying one does not perform ablution because of it - so they became confused to me. Among those who said ablution is required from what fire has touched were Abu Salamah, 'Umar ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz, Umm Habibah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Zayd ibn Thabit from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Sufyan said: And al-Zuhri narrated to us, telling us that 'Ali ibn Abd Allah ibn 'Abbas informed him from his father, and Ja'far ibn 'Amr ibn Umayyah al-Damri from his father: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cut meat from the shoulder of a sheep and ate from it, then stood for prayer and prayed without performing ablution. And the other said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate meat and prayed without performing ablution. I have no doubt that al-Zuhri narrated to us from both of them; I only doubt because I do not distinguish the hadith of one from the hadith of the other. Sufyan said: And al-Zuhri used to perform ablution from what fire had touched."
"920","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, saying: Sufyan ibn Sa'id al-Thawri narrated to us - Sufyan said: and this is the best we found with him - saying: Bukayr ibn 'Ata' al-Laythi informed me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ya'mar al-Dili, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Hajj is 'Arafat. Whoever reaches 'Arafah before dawn has reached Hajj. The days of Mina are three; whoever hastens in two days, there is no sin upon him, and whoever delays, there is no sin upon him."
"921","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, who said: I heard 'Urwah ibn Mudarris ibn Aws ibn Harithah ibn Lam al-Ta'i saying: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at al-Muzdalifah and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have come from the two mountains of Tayyi', and by Allah, I did not come until I exhausted myself and wore out my mount, and I left no hill without standing upon it. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever witnesses this prayer with us, having stood at 'Arafah before that by night or day, his Hajj is complete and he has fulfilled his rites."
"922","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us - he said: and he was the most retentive of the two for this hadith - from al-Sha'bi, who said: I heard 'Urwah ibn Mudarris ibn Aws ibn Harithah ibn Lam al-Ta'i saying: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at al-Muzdalifah and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have come to you just now from the two mountains of Tayyi', having exhausted my mount and wearied myself. Is there any Hajj for me? Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever witnesses this prayer with us and stands with us until we depart, having stood before that at 'Arafah by night or day, his Hajj is complete and he has fulfilled his rites."
"923","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: I heard al-Zuhri reporting from the son of Suraqah or the nephew of Suraqah, from Suraqah, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at al-Ji'ranah, and I did not know what to ask him about, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, I fill my watering trough waiting for my camels to come to me, then stray camels come and drink. Is there any reward for me in that? Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For you there is a reward in every living creature with a moist liver. Sufyan said: This is what I retained from al-Zuhri, though part of its beginning became confused to me, and Wa'il ibn Dawud informed me of some of these words from al-Zuhri; I cannot separate what I retained from al-Zuhri from what Wa'il told me. Suraqah said: I came to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was at al-Ji'ranah, and I would not pass by any detachment of the Ansar's cavalry without them striking my head and saying: Get away, get away. When I reached him, I raised the document and said: It is I, O Messenger of Allah. He had written for me a guarantee of safety on a slip of paper, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes, today is a day of fidelity, righteousness, and truthfulness."
"924","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: al-Zuhri narrated to us, saying: I heard al-A'raj narrating from Ibn Buhaynah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in a prayer - I think it was 'Asr - and he stood up in the second rak'ah without sitting. When he was at the end of his prayer, he prostrated two prostrations before giving salam."
"925","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: And Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from al-A'raj, from Ibn Buhaynah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly, except that he said: He stood up in the rak'ah in which one rests for sitting. And sometimes Sufyan would say: Abd Allah ibn Buhaynah, and sometimes he would say: Abd Allah ibn Malik ibn Buhaynah."
"926","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, having heard it from Sa'id ibn Abi Hind, having heard it from Mutarrif ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir, who said: I heard 'Uthman ibn Abi al-'As al-Thaqafi saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Lead your people in prayer and measure them by their weakest, for among them are the elderly, the weak, and those with needs."
"927","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: al-Fudayl ibn 'Iyad narrated to us, from Ash'ath, from al-Hasan, from 'Uthman ibn Abi al-'As, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: And appoint a caller to prayer who does not take a wage for his call."
"928","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Qa'nab al-Tamimi - and he was trustworthy and excellent - narrated to us, from 'Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Buraydah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The sanctity of the women of the warriors upon those who stay behind is like that of their mothers in sanctity. There is no man among those who stay behind who betrays a warrior concerning his family except that he will be set up for him on the Day of Resurrection and it will be said to him: O so-and-so, this is so-and-so the son of so-and-so who betrayed you, so take from his good deeds whatever you wish. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to us and said: So what do you think?"
"929","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Abu Ghalib, the keeper of the whip, narrated to us, saying: I saw Abu Umamah al-Bahili notice the heads of the Khawarij on the steps of Damascus, and he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Dogs of the people of Hellfire, dogs of the people of Hellfire, dogs of the people of Hellfire. Then he wept and said: The worst slain beneath the canopy of the sky, and the best slain are those whom they kill. Abu Ghalib said: Did you yourself hear this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes, for then I would indeed be bold; I heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) more than once, not twice nor thrice."
"930","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Muttarih Abu al-Muhallab narrated to us, from 'Ubayd Allah ibn Zahr, from al-Qasim Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most enviable of my beloved ones in station with me is a believing man of light means, with a share of prayer; though obscure among people, his death comes swiftly, few weep for him, and his inheritance is small."
"931","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Muttarih Abu al-Muhallab narrated to us, from 'Ubayd Allah ibn Zahr, from al-Qasim Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The price of a singing slave-girl is unlawful, as are her sale, her purchase, and listening to her."
"932","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn 'Alqamah al-Laythi narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Bilal ibn al-Harith al-Muzani, conveying it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: A man may utter a word from the wrath of Allah without thinking it will reach what it reaches, and Allah records His wrath against him because of it until the Day of Resurrection. And a man may utter a word from the pleasure of Allah without thinking it will reach what it reaches, and Allah records His pleasure for him because of it until the Day of Resurrection. Al-Humaydi said: This is what I have, conveying it as he used to say it at first."
"933","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: 'Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Minhal informed me, saying: I heard Iyas ibn 'Abd al-Muzani - when he saw people selling water - saying: Do not sell water, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbidding the sale of water. 'Amr ibn Dinar said: And I do not know which water it is. Sufyan said: In our view it is that it be sold at the place where Allah brought it forth, and it has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he forbade the sale of surplus well water."
"934","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from 'Adi ibn Hatim, who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about hunting with the mi'rad, and he said: Do not eat except what you slaughter properly."
"935","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Mujalid narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from 'Adi ibn Hatim, who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about hunting with the mi'rad, and he said: What it strikes with its edge, eat; what it strikes with its side, do not eat, for it is killed by a blow."
"936","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Mujalid narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from 'Adi ibn Hatim, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How will you be when a lone woman traveler comes from the farthest Yemen to the palaces of al-Hirah fearing none but Allah? I said: O Messenger of Allah, what about Tayyi' with its horsemen and men? He said: Allah will suffice against Tayyi' and all others. Mujalid said: And indeed a lone woman traveler used to set out from Hadramawt until she reached al-Hirah."
"937","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from 'Adi ibn Hatim, who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about fasting, and he said: Until the white thread becomes distinct from the black thread. 'Adi said: So I took two ropes, one white and the other black, and began looking at them. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said something. Sufyan said: Something I did not retain, and he said: It is only night and day. It was said to Sufyan: Did you hear this from Mujalid? He said: Yes, and he used to render it well, but I did not retain all of it."
"938","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from 'Adi ibn Hatim, who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about hunting with a trained dog, and he said: When you release your trained dog and mention the name of Allah, eat from what it holds for you. If it eats, do not eat, for it held only for itself. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what if other dogs mix with our dogs? He said: You mentioned the name of Allah only over your dog."
"939","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Abu Farwah al-Hamdani narrated to us, saying: I heard al-Sha'bi saying: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir upon the pulpit saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Lawful is clear, unlawful is clear, and there are doubtful matters between them. Whoever leaves what seems doubtful to him of sin will be even more avoidant of what is clear to him, and whoever ventures upon what he doubts is close to falling into the unlawful. Every king has a sanctuary, and the sanctuary of Allah on earth is His acts of disobedience."
"940","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Mujalid narrated to us, saying: I heard al-Sha'bi saying: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir saying upon the pulpit: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - al-Sha'bi said: Whenever I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir upon the pulpit saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I thought I would never hear anyone after him saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The example of the believers in their mutual generosity, affection, and mercy is like the human being: when one of his limbs complains, the rest of his body responds with fever and sleeplessness."
"941","He said: And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: In the human being there is a morsel of flesh: when it is sound and healthy, the rest of the body is sound and healthy for it; and when it is diseased, the rest of the body is diseased and corrupted for it; and it is the heart."
"942","And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The example of the one who compromises regarding the rights of Allah, the one who falls into them, and the one who upholds them is like three men who boarded a ship and drew lots for its places. One of them got its lowest, roughest, and worst part, and his coming and going and his pouring of water affected them. While they were in it, they were suddenly surprised by him having seized an adze. They said to him: What are you doing? He said: I will make a hole in my own portion so it is nearer for me to water, with my coming and going and my pouring of water in it. Some of them said: Leave him - may Allah cast him away - to make a hole in his portion as he wishes. Others said: Do not let him pierce it, lest he destroy us and destroy himself. If they seize his hand, he is saved and they are saved with him; and if they do not seize his hand, he perishes and they perish with him."
"943","He said: And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Lawful is clear, unlawful is clear, and there are doubtful matters between them. Whoever leaves what seems doubtful to him of sin will be even more avoidant of what is clear to him, and whoever ventures upon what he doubts is close to falling into the unlawful - like one who grazes beside a sanctuary, close to falling into it. Every king has a sanctuary, and the sanctuary of Allah on earth is His acts of disobedience."
"944","He said: And I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir saying: My father granted me a slave boy, and my mother 'Amrah bint Rawahah said to him: Go to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and take him as witness. So he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to take him as witness, and he said: Have you granted each of your children the like of this? He said: No. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I bear witness only to what is right. And he refused to bear witness to it."
"945","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir narrated to us, from his father, from Habib ibn Salim, from his father, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir - al-Humaydi said: Sufyan used to err in it - that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the Eid prayer: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, and: Has there reached you the story of the Overwhelming? And he used to recite them in both when that coincided with Friday."
"946","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Jarir ibn 'Abd al-Hamid al-Dabbi narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn al-Muntashir, from his father, from Habib ibn Salim, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with similar meaning, except that he did not mention in it: from his father."
"947","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: al-Zuhri narrated to us, saying: Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman and Muhammad ibn al-Nu'man informed me, that they both heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir narrating: that his father granted him a gift, and he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to take him as witness. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Have you granted each of your children the like of this? He said: No. He said: Then take it back."
"948","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Dawud ibn Qays al-Farra' narrated to us, from 'Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Aqram al-Khuza'i, from his father, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at al-Qa' in Namirah praying, and I saw the whiteness of his armpits when he prostrated."
"949","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: al-Zuhri narrated to us, saying: I heard Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi saying: A man peered through a hole into the room of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) held an iron comb with which he was scratching his head. He said: Had I known you were looking, I would have thrust it into your eye. Seeking permission was only prescribed because of sight."
"950","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Abu Hazim narrated to us, that he heard Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been sent, I and the Hour, like this from this. And Sufyan pointed with the index and middle fingers."
"951","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Abu Hazim told us: They asked Sahl ibn Sa'd: From what was the pulpit of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made? He said: No one among people remains more knowledgeable about it than I. It is from the tamarisk of al-Ghabah; so-and-so, the freedman of so-and-so, made it for him. I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he ascended it: he faced the qiblah, said the takbir, recited, bowed, then descended backwards and prostrated, then ascended and recited, then bowed, then descended backwards and prostrated."
"952","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Abu Hazim narrated to us, saying: I heard Sahl ibn Sa'd saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to reconcile between Banu 'Amr ibn 'Awf concerning a dispute that occurred among them, until they threw stones at one another. Prayer time came; Bilal called the adhan, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was delayed, and Abu Bakr stepped forward leading the people in prayer. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, making his way through the rows. When he reached the row next to Abu Bakr, the people began clapping. Abu Bakr was a man who would not turn in prayer; when he heard that, he turned and saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gestured to him to remain in place, but Abu Bakr raised his head to the sky, thanked Allah, and stepped back. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stepped forward, and when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) completed his prayer, he said: O Abu Bakr, what prevented you when I gestured to you? He said: It was not for the son of Abu Quhafah to be seen in front of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to the people and said: O people, what is the matter with you that when something happens to you in your prayer, you take to clapping? Clapping is for women and glorification is for men. Whoever is afflicted by something in his prayer, let him say: Glory be to Allah."
"953","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Abu Hazim narrated to us, that he heard Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi saying: I was among the people with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a woman came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have offered myself to you, so consider my case. A man stood up and said: Marry her to me, O Messenger of Allah, if you have no need of her. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained silent. Then she stood and said the like of that, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the man: Do you have anything to give her? He said: No. He said: Go and seek something. So he went and came back and said: O Messenger of Allah, I found nothing. He said: Go and seek, even an iron ring. So he went and came back and said: O Messenger of Allah, I found nothing, not even an iron ring. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you have anything of the Qur'an with you? He said: Yes, such-and-such surah and such-and-such surah. He said: Then go, for I have married her to you for what you have of the Qur'an."
"954","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Abu Hazim narrated to us, saying: The people differed about with what the wound of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was treated on the day of Uhud, so they asked Sahl - and he was among the last of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remaining in Madinah - and he said: No one among people remains more knowledgeable about it than I. Fatimah would wash the blood from the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), 'Ali would bring water in his shield, a mat was taken and burned, and his wound was stuffed with it."
"955","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Abu Hazim narrated to us, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The space of a whip in Paradise is better than the world and what is in it."
"956","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Maysarah narrated to us: Wahb ibn Abd Allah ibn Qarib - or Marib - informed me, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the Farewell Hajj saying: May Allah have mercy upon those who shave. And he gestured with his hand thus, and al-Humaydi extended his right hand. They said: O Messenger of Allah, and those who shorten? He said: May Allah have mercy upon those who shave. They said: O Messenger of Allah, and those who shorten? He said: May Allah have mercy upon those who shave. They said: O Messenger of Allah, and those who shorten? Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And those who shorten. And al-Humaydi gestured with his hand but did not extend it as at first. Sufyan said: I found in my book from Ibrahim ibn Maysarah, from Wahb ibn Abd Allah ibn Marib - while my memory is Qarib - and people say Qarib as I memorized, so I say Qarib or Marib."
"957","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Dawud ibn Yazid Abu Yazid al-Awdi narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Khanbash, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: An 'umrah in the month of Ramadan is like a Hajj."
"958","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, saying: al-Zuhri narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib informed me, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the reciter says amin, say amin, for the angels say amin. Whoever's amin coincides with the amin of the angels, his past sins are forgiven."
"959","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: I heard al-Zuhri - and I memorized it from him - from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, that he informed him, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When it is Friday, there are angels at every gate of the mosque writing down the people in their order, the first then the first. When the imam comes out, the scrolls are folded and they listen to the sermon. The one who comes early to Friday is like one who offers a camel, then the next like one who offers a cow, then the next like one who offers a ram - until he mentioned the chicken and the egg. Abu Bakr said: It was said to Sufyan: They mention in this hadith from al-Agharr, from Abu Hurayrah. Sufyan said: I never heard al-Zuhri mention al-Agharr at all; I only heard him saying it from Sa'id, that he informed him from Abu Hurayrah."
"960","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us: I heard al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you come to prayer, do not come to it running; come to it walking, with tranquility upon you. What you catch, pray; and what you miss, complete."
"961","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: I heard al-Zuhri saying: Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib informed me, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The fitrah is five - or five are of the fitrah: circumcision, shaving the pubic hair, trimming the nails, plucking the armpits, and trimming the mustache."
"962","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: I heard al-Zuhri narrating from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: A man stood and asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): May one of us pray in a single garment? Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Does each of you have two garments? And Abu Hurayrah said to a man asking him: Do you know Abu Hurayrah? For he prays in a single garment while his clothes lie placed upon the rack."
"963","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: al-Zuhri narrated to us as I tell you, needing no one else regarding it, saying: Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib informed me, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: A Bedouin entered the mosque while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting. He said: Then he stood and prayed, and when he finished his prayer he said: O Allah, have mercy upon me and Muhammad, and have mercy upon no one else with us. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to him and said: You have restricted what is vast. Soon after, he urinated in the mosque, and the people hastened toward him. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pour over it a bucket of water, or a pail of water. Then he said: You have been sent as facilitators and were not sent as those who cause hardship."
"964","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: al-Zuhri narrated to us, saying: And I memorized it from him, saying: Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib informed me, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his head from the last rak'ah of the morning prayer, he said: O Allah, save al-Walid ibn al-Walid, Salamah ibn Hisham, 'Ayyash ibn Abi Rabi'ah, and the oppressed in Makkah. O Allah, make Your grip severe upon Mudar, and make it years upon them like the years of Yusuf."
"965","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers in other mosques except the Sacred Mosque."
"966","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Ziyad ibn Sa'd narrated to us, saying: Sulayman ibn 'Atiq informed me, saying: I heard Ibn al-Zubayr upon the pulpit saying: I heard 'Umar ibn al-Khattab saying: A prayer in the Sacred Mosque is better than a hundred prayers in other mosques. Al-Humaydi said: Sufyan said: So they hold that prayer in the Sacred Mosque is better than a hundred thousand prayers in other mosques except the mosque of the Messenger, for he favored it over others by a hundred prayers."
"967","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: al-Zuhri narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib informed me, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the heat intensifies, cool down the prayer, for the intensity of heat is from the blast of Hell."
"968","And he said: The Fire complained to its Lord, saying: My Lord, parts of me have consumed one another. So He permitted it two breaths: a breath in winter and a breath in summer. The most intense heat you feel is from its heat, and the most intense cold you feel is from its bitter cold."
"969","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Saddles are not tied except to three mosques: the Sacred Mosque, this mosque of mine, and al-Aqsa Mosque."
"970","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Abd al-'Aziz ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, saying: Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn Usamah ibn al-Had narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: Basrah ibn Abi Basrah al-Ghifari informed me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Mounts are not readied except to three mosques: the Sacred Mosque, this mosque of mine, and the mosque of Bayt al-Maqdis."
"971","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: al-Zuhri narrated to us, from one who heard Abu Hurayrah - either Sa'id or Abu Salamah, most often saying it from Sa'id - from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been given five that no one before me was given: the whole earth has been made for me a mosque and a means of purification, I have been aided with awe, war spoils have been made lawful for me, I have been sent to the red and the black, and I have been given intercession."
"972","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: al-Zuhri narrated to us, saying: Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever catches a rak'ah of a prayer has caught it."
"973","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: al-Zuhri narrated to us, saying: Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Satan comes to one of you in his prayer and confuses his prayer for him until he does not know how much he has prayed. If one of you finds that, let him prostrate two prostrations while sitting."
"974","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: al-Zuhri narrated to us, saying: Abu Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Glorification in prayer is for men, and clapping is for women."
"975","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: I heard al-Zuhri narrating from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has never listened to anything as He listens to a prophet chanting the Qur'an."
"976","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: al-Zuhri narrated to us, saying: Abu Salamah informed me, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fasts Ramadan with faith and seeking reward, his past sins are forgiven; and whoever stands in prayer on the Night of Decree with faith and seeking reward, his past sins are forgiven."
"977","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you wakes from sleep, let him not dip his hand into the vessel until he washes it three times, for he does not know where his hand spent the night."
"978","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly. Sufyan said: This supports the view of those who say ablution is required from touching the private part."
"979","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: al-Zuhri narrated to us, saying: I heard Ibn Ukaymah al-Laythi narrating to Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, saying: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in the morning prayer, and when the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) finished, he said: Has any of you recited along with me? A man said: Yes, I have. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I say, why is the Qur'an being contested with me? Sufyan said: Then al-Zuhri said something I did not understand, and Ma'mar later told me that he said: So the people refrained from reciting in what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited aloud. Abu Bakr said: And Sufyan used to say regarding this hadith: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in a prayer - I think it was the morning prayer - for a time; then Sufyan said to us: I looked in my book and found therein with me: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in the morning prayer."
"980","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We are the last, and we are the foremost, in that they were given the Book before us and we were given it after them. This is the day concerning which they differed, and Allah guided us to it. People follow us in it: the Jews tomorrow and the Christians the day after."
"981","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: And Ibn Tawus narrated it to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly, except that he said: In that - its explanation being: because they."
"982","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I had intended to establish the prayer, the 'Isha' prayer, then command my youths to go to the houses of people who stay back from the 'Isha' prayer and burn them down upon them with bundles of firewood. If one of them knew he would find two good meaty bones or a fat bone, he would attend the prayer."
"983","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you cleans himself with stones, let him do so an odd number of times; and when he blows his nose, let him do so an odd number of times."
"984","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The imam is a leader; if he prays sitting, pray sitting, and if he prays standing, pray standing."
"985","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said the like of it, except that he said: For the commander is his imam."
"986","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Satan ties three knots upon the back of the head of one of you, striking upon the place of each knot: A long night is upon you, so sleep. If he awakens during the night and remembers Allah the Exalted, one knot is undone; if he performs ablution, two knots are undone; if he prays, all the knots are undone, and he rises fresh of spirit and energetic. Otherwise, he rises foul of spirit and lazy."
"987","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you see this qiblah of mine? Neither your bowing nor your humility - or your bowing nor your prostration - is hidden from me."
"988","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Dawud ibn Shabur, Humayd al-A'raj, and Ibn Abi Najih narrated to us, from Mujahid, regarding the saying of Allah the Mighty and Majestic: And your turning among those who prostrate - he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to see behind him in prayer as he saw in front of him."
"989","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you say: O Allah, forgive me if You will; O Allah, have mercy upon me if You will. Rather, let him ask with resolve, for there is none who compels Him - or he said: none who coerces Him."
"990","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you pray in a single garment with nothing of it upon his shoulder."
"991","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not that I would cause hardship for the believers, I would command them to delay the 'Isha' prayer, and to use the tooth-stick at every prayer."
"992","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman al-A'raj informed me, saying: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you say to your companion on Friday while the imam is delivering the sermon: Be quiet - you have engaged in idle speech. Abu al-Zinad said: This is the dialect of Abu Hurayrah; it is properly laghawta."
"993","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a dog laps from the vessel of one of you, let him wash it seven times."
"994","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah similarly, raising it once, except that he said: The first of them - or one of them - with dust."
"995","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, saying: Musa ibn Abi 'Uthman informed me, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you urinate into stagnant water and then bathe from it."
"996","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Ayyub narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you urinate into stagnant water that does not flow and then bathe from it."
"997","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: 'Asim ibn 'Ubayd Allah al-'Umari narrated to us, from a freedman of Abu Ruhm, who said: Abu Hurayrah met a perfumed woman and said: Where are you heading, O female servant of the Almighty? She said: The mosque. He said: And did you perfume yourself for it? She said: Yes. He said: Go back and wash, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Any woman who perfumes herself then goes out intending the mosque, no prayer is accepted from her, nor such-and-such, until she returns and washes herself as she washes from major impurity."
"998","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Sumayy, the freedman of Abu Bakr, narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to seek refuge from the strain of affliction, being overtaken by misery, evil decree, and the gloating of enemies. Sufyan said: Three of these four."
"999","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: al-'Ala' ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Ya'qub, the freedman of al-Huraqah, narrated to me, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah the Exalted said: I have divided prayer between Me and My servant. When the servant says: All praise belongs to Allah, Lord of the worlds - Allah the Mighty and Majestic says: My servant has praised Me. When he says: The Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate - He says: My servant has extolled Me, or: My servant has glorified Me. When the servant says: Master of the Day of Judgment - He says: My servant has entrusted himself to Me. When he says: You alone we worship, and You alone we ask for help - this is between Me and My servant, and for My servant is what he asks. When he says: Guide us along the Straight Path, the path of those upon whom You have bestowed favor, not of those who earned anger nor of those who went astray - this is for My servant, and for My servant is what he asks."
"1000","1004 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan, Abd al-Aziz al-Darawardi, and Ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, from al-Ala, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every prayer in which the Opening of the Book (al-Fatihah) is not recited is deficient, it is deficient. Abd al-Rahman said: So I said to Abu Hurayrah: But I hear the recitation of the imam. He nudged me with his hand and said: O Persian - or he said: O son of the Persian - recite it to yourself."
"1001","1005 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, from Abu Salih, that he heard Abu Hurayrah - on one occasion raising it (to the Prophet) - say: Deeds are presented on every Monday and Thursday, and Allah Almighty forgives on those two days every person who does not associate anything with Allah, except a man between whom and his brother there is enmity. It is said: Leave these two until they reconcile, leave these two until they reconcile."
"1002","1006 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Suhayl ibn Abi Salih narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to pray four (rakahs) after Friday prayer. Sufyan said: And others besides me said that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever among you prays after Friday prayer, let him pray four. And this is better, but what I memorized is the first."
"1003","1007 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from Said al-Maqburi, who said: A man said to Abu Hurayrah: I am a man with much hair, and three handfuls (of water) are not enough for me. So he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had more hair than you and was more pleasant-smelling than you; he used to pour three handfuls over his head."
"1004","1008 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Alqamah narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not prevent the female servants of Allah from the mosques of Allah, and let them not go out except unattractive (without adornment or perfume)."
"1005","1009 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah Almighty bestows blessing upon people in the morning and in the evening, yet some of them wake up disbelieving in it, saying: We were given rain by such-and-such star. Muhammad ibn Ibrahim said: So I narrated it to Said ibn al-Musayyib, and he said: We have heard this from Abu Hurayrah, but one who witnessed Umar leading the people in prayer for rain informed me that he said: O Abbas, O uncle of the Messenger of Allah, how much remains of the rising of the Pleiades? He said: The knowledgeable ones about it claim that it appears on the horizon seven (nights) after its setting. He said: Then the seventh had not passed before we were given rain."
"1006","1010 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Tawus narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek refuge in Allah from the punishment of Allah, seek refuge in Allah from the trial of life and death, seek refuge in Allah from the punishment of the grave, seek refuge in Allah from the trial of the False Messiah, the Dajjal."
"1007","1011 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Tawus, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with a similar narration."
"1008","1012 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with a similar narration."
"1009","1013 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in one of the two afternoon prayers - either Zuhr or Asr, and my stronger thought is that it was Asr - two rakahs, then he went to a tree trunk in the mosque and leaned against it while angry. The hasty people went out saying: The prayer has been shortened, the prayer has been shortened. Among the people were Abu Bakr and Umar, but they were too awed to speak to him. So Dhu al-Yadayn stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, has the prayer been shortened or did you forget? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is Dhu al-Yadayn saying? They said: He is right. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in two rakahs, then gave the greeting of peace, then said the takbir and prostrated like his prostration (in prayer) or longer, then raised his head, then said the takbir and prostrated, then said the takbir and raised his head. Muhammad said: And I was informed on the authority of Imran ibn Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: And he gave the greeting of peace."
"1010","1014 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Labid narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, with a narration similar to the hadith of Ayyub, and he added in it: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked to the right and to the left and said: What is Dhu al-Yadayn saying?"
"1011","1015 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you rises at night, let him pray two brief rakahs with which he opens his prayer."
"1012","1016 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed there is in Friday an hour which no Muslim servant meets while standing in prayer asking Allah Almighty for good in it except that He gives it to him. And he gestured with his hand indicating its brevity, and Sufyan clenched (his fingers) saying: A little."
"1013","1017 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from his father, who said: I came to Madinah and stayed with Abu Hurayrah, and there was kinship between him and my masters. Abu Hurayrah used to lead the people in prayer and lighten it. So I said: O Abu Hurayrah, was this the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes, and shorter."
"1014","1018 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from al-Qaqa, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am to you only like a father, teaching you. So when one of you goes to relieve himself, let him not face the qiblah nor turn his back to it while defecating or urinating. And he commanded us to clean ourselves with three stones, and he forbade dung and decayed bones, and that a man clean himself with his right hand."
"1015","1019 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Alqamah narrated to us, he said: I heard Malih ibn Abd Allah al-Sadi narrating from Abu Hurayrah, who said: Indeed the one who raises his head and lowers it before the imam, his forelock is in the hand of a devil. Abu Bakr said: And Sufyan would sometimes raise it (to the Prophet) and sometimes not raise it."
"1016","1020 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ata, who said: We heard Abu Hurayrah saying: In every prayer I recite; whatever the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made audible to us, we make audible to you, and whatever he concealed from us, we conceal from you. Every prayer in which the Mother of the Quran is not recited is deficient. A man said to him: What if I recite it alone, does it suffice me? He said: If you stop at it, it suffices you, but if you add more, that is better."
"1017","1021 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn Musa narrated to us, from Ata ibn Mina, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: We prostrated with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in (the surahs) When the heaven is split asunder and Read in the name of your Lord. Sufyan said: And Ata ibn Mina was among the well-known companions of Abu Hurayrah."
"1018","1022 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, from Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: We prostrated with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in (the surahs) When the heaven is split asunder and Read in the name of your Lord who created. Al-Humaydi said: It was said to Sufyan: Including Read in the name of your Lord? He said: Yes."
"1019","1023 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Umayyah narrated to us, from Abu Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hurayth al-Udhri, from his grandfather, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: Abu al-Qasim, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), said: When one of you prays, let him place something in front of his face; if he does not find anything, let him set up a staff; if he does not find a staff, let him draw a line, then whatever passes in front of him will not harm him."
"1020","1024 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Hakim ibn Jubayr narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Everything has a pinnacle, and the pinnacle of the Quran is Surah al-Baqarah. In it there is a verse, the chief of the verses of the Quran: it is not recited in a house in which there is a devil except that he leaves it - Ayat al-Kursi."
"1021","1025 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Umayyah narrated to us, he said: A Bedouin from the desert people narrated to me, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you recites I swear by the Day of Resurrection and reaches its end, Is He not able to give life to the dead, let him say: Yes indeed. And when he recites By those sent forth in succession and reaches its end, In what message after it will they believe, let him say: We believe in Allah. And when he recites By the fig and the olive and reaches its end, Is not Allah the most just of judges, let him say: Yes indeed. And sometimes Sufyan would say: Yes indeed, and I am among the witnesses to that. Sufyan said: Ismail said: So I asked the Bedouin to repeat the hadith, and he said: O son of my brother, do you think I did not memorize it? I have performed sixty pilgrimages, and there is not one pilgrimage among them except that I know the camel upon which I performed it."
"1022","1026 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Yazid narrated to us, he said: One who heard Abu Hurayrah informed me that he said: Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is in a state of major impurity should not sleep until he performs ablution as for prayer."
"1023","1027 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to us, he said: I heard a man saying: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying standing and sitting, and barefoot and wearing sandals, and I saw him turning (after prayer) to his right and to his left. Sufyan said: They said: This is Abu al-Awbar."
"1024","1028 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Said ibn Masruq al-Thawri narrated to us, from Ashath ibn Sulaym al-Muharibi, from his father, who said: Abu Hurayrah was sitting in the mosque when he saw a man leaving the mosque after the call to prayer, so he said: As for this one, he has disobeyed Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1025","1029 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The imam is a guarantor and the caller to prayer is entrusted. O Allah, guide the imams and forgive the callers to prayer."
"1026","1030 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from his father - or from Said al-Maqburi - from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best rows of men are the first of them and the worst of them are the last of them, and the best rows of women are the last of them and the worst of them are the first of them."
"1027","1031 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Raja narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with a similar narration."
"1028","1032 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Sumayy, the freedman of Abu Bakr, narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: An accepted Hajj has no reward except Paradise, and one Umrah to the next expiates what is between them."
"1029","1033 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Abi Uthman informed me, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a man driving a sacrificial camel and said: Ride it. He said: It is a sacrificial animal. He said: Ride it. He said: It is a sacrificial animal. He said: Ride it, woe to you - or: woe unto you, ride it."
"1030","1034 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Mansur ibn al-Mutamir narrated to us, from Abu Hazim al-Ashjai, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever performs Hajj to this House and does not engage in obscenity nor wickedness until he returns, returns as on the day his mother bore him."
"1031","1035 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: Hanzalah al-Aslami informed me, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in whose Hand is my soul, the son of Maryam will surely enter ihram at the valley of al-Rawha as a pilgrim or as one performing Umrah, or he will combine both."
"1032","1036 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from Said, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman should not travel more than three (days' distance) except with a mahram."
"1033","1037 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fasts Ramadan with faith and seeking reward will be forgiven what has preceded of his sins, and whoever stands (in prayer) on the Night of Decree with faith and seeking reward will be forgiven what has preceded of his sins."
"1034","1038 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Al-Zuhri narrated to us, and I memorized it from him, he said: Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me, from Abu Hurayrah: That a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am ruined. He said: What is the matter with you? He said: I had intercourse with my wife in Ramadan. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Can you free a slave? He said: No. He said: Can you fast two consecutive months? He said: No. He said: Can you feed sixty poor persons? He said: No, I cannot find (the means). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sit down. So he sat, and while he was like that, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a large basket containing dates - and al-araq is the huge basket - so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Go and give this in charity. He said: O Messenger of Allah, upon one poorer than us? By the One who sent you with the truth, there is no household between its two lava plains poorer than us. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed until his eyeteeth appeared - and sometimes Sufyan would say: his molar teeth - then he said: Go and feed your family with it."
"1035","1039 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not fast continuously without breaking fast. They said: O Messenger of Allah, but you fast continuously? He said: I am not like any one of you; I spend the night with my Lord feeding me and giving me drink."
"1036","1040 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: Every deed of the son of Adam is for him except fasting; it is for Me, and I reward for it."
"1037","1041 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Ubayd ibn Umayr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with a similar narration."
"1038","1042 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you is invited to food while he is fasting, let him say: I am fasting."
"1039","1043 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with a similar narration."
"1040","1044 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you wakes up in the morning fasting, let him not engage in obscenity nor act ignorantly; if a man insults him or fights him, let him say: I am fasting."
"1041","1045 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with a similar narration."
"1042","1046 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Abi Uthman informed me, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman should not fast a day outside the month of Ramadan while her husband is present except with his permission."
"1043","1047 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Jadah informed me, from Abd Allah ibn Amr al-Qari, who said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: I did not forbid fasting on Friday, but Muhammad - by the Lord of this House - forbade it."
"1044","1048 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, Yahya ibn Jadah informed me, from Abd Allah ibn Amr al-Qari, who said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: It was not I who said: Whoever wakes up in a state of major impurity has broken his fast. But Muhammad - by the Lord of this Kabah - said it."
"1045","1049 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Suhayl ibn Abi Salih narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah: That some women said: O Messenger of Allah, we cannot reach your gathering because of the men, so would you appoint for us a time when we come to you? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your appointment is the house of so-and-so woman. So they came at his appointed time, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, and among what he told them was that he said: There is no woman who loses three children and bears it patiently seeking reward except that she enters Paradise. A woman said: Or two, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Or two."
"1046","1050 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: I heard it from the mouth of Ibn Shihab al-Zuhri, he said: Said ibn al-Musayyib informed me, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No Muslim loses three children and enters the Fire except to fulfill the oath (i.e., briefly passing over Hell)."
"1047","1051 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Sumayy, the freedman of Abu Bakr, narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays over a funeral has a qirat, and whoever follows it until its matter is completed has two qirats, one of them like (Mount) Uhud."
"1048","1052 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Zuhri narrating from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hasten with the funeral, for if it was righteous, it is good you are advancing it to, and if it was other than that, it is evil you are putting off your necks."
"1049","1053 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: When the Negus died, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek forgiveness for him."
"1050","1054 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from Wahb ibn Kaysan, from one who heard Abu Hurayrah saying: Umar ibn al-Khattab heard the voice of a weeping woman and forbade her, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Leave her, O Abu Hafs, for the covenant (of death) is recent, and the eye is weeping, and the soul is afflicted."
"1051","1055 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Hamzah ibn al-Mughirah al-Kufi - and he was among the leaders of the freedmen - narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, do not make my grave an idol. May Allah curse people who took the graves of their prophets as mosques."
"1052","1056 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: Said ibn al-Musayyib narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not engage in najsh (false bidding), and let not a man sell upon the sale of his brother, nor propose upon the proposal of his brother, nor let a town-dweller sell for a Bedouin, and let not a woman ask for the divorce of her sister so that she may overturn what is in her vessel."
"1053","1057 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not meet the caravans for trade, and do not engage in najsh, and let not a town-dweller sell for a Bedouin, and let not a man sell upon the sale of his brother, nor propose upon the proposal of his brother."
"1054","1058 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not tie up the udders of camels and sheep for sale. Whoever among you buys any of that has the better of the two options: if he wishes he may keep it, and if he wishes he may return it along with a sa of dates, not of wheat."
"1055","1059 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, who said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever buys a musarrah (an animal whose milk was withheld) has the choice: if he wishes he may keep it, and if he wishes he may return it along with a sa of dates, not of wheat."
"1056","1060 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Al-Ala narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A false oath promotes the commodity but wipes out the profit."
"1057","1061 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Abu Damrah narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Yazid al-Ayli, from Ibn Shihab, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with a similar narration."
"1058","1062 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Delaying payment by a rich man is injustice; when one of you is referred to a solvent man, let him accept the transfer."
"1059","1063 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a man selling food which pleased him, so he put his hand into it and found it was damp food. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He who deceives us is not of us."
"1060","1064 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Salim Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, from a man, from Abu Hurayrah: That a man used to gift the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) every year a waterskin of wine, so one year he gifted it to him after it had been forbidden. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It has been forbidden. The man said: Shall I not sell it? He said: Indeed the One who forbade drinking it forbade selling it. He said: Shall I not gift it to the Jews? He said: Indeed the One who forbade it forbade gifting it to the Jews. He said: What shall I do with it? He said: Pour it out in the open ground."
"1061","1065 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Yahya al-Makhzumi informed me, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any man who finds his own goods intact with a man who has gone bankrupt has more right to them."
"1062","1066 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, from Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with a similar narration."
"1063","1067 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My likeness and the likeness of the prophets before me is like that of a man who built a building and made it excellent, complete, and beautiful, except for the place of one brick. So people began going around it saying: We have never seen a building more beautiful than this except for the place of this brick. Indeed I was that brick."
"1064","1068 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My likeness and the likeness of people is like that of a man who kindled a fire; when it lit up for him, insects and moths began falling into it. So I am holding you back by your waistbands from the Fire while you plunge into it."
"1065","1069 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not that I would cause hardship to the believers, I would not send a detachment without staying behind from it; I do not have mounts to carry them upon, and it is hard upon me that they stay behind after me."
"1066","1070 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in whose Hand is my soul, I would love to be killed in the cause of Allah, then brought to life, then killed, then brought to life, then killed. Abu Hurayrah said three times: I bear witness, by Allah."
"1067","1071 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, I take with You a covenant which You will never break: any Muslim man whom I harm - whether I flog him or curse him - make it for him a prayer, a purification, and a supplication for him. Abu al-Zinad said: This is the dialect of Abu Hurayrah, and it is actually: I flogged him, I cursed him."
"1068","1072 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no newborn except that Satan pricks him in his shoulder blade, except Isa and his mother, for the angels surrounded them both. And recite if you wish: And I seek refuge with You for her and her offspring from Satan, the accursed."
"1069","1073 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Yazid narrated to us, from Nafi ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in part of the day, he not speaking to me nor I to him, until he came to the market of Qaynuqa, then he turned back until he came to the courtyard of Aishah and sat in it, then he said: Is he there, is he there? - meaning Hasan. I thought that his mother was only keeping him to wash him and dress him in a necklace. He did not tarry before he came running until each of them embraced the other. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, I love him, so love him and love whoever loves him."
"1070","1074 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People follow Quraysh in this matter: their Muslims follow their Muslims, and their disbelievers follow their disbelievers."
"1071","1075 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You find people to be mines: the best of them in the pre-Islamic age are the best of them in Islam when they gain understanding."
"1072","1076 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Tumah ibn Amr al-Jafari narrated to me, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with a similar narration."
"1073","1077 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ... (The chain, ha.)."
"1074","1078 - And Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Tawus narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best women who rode camels. One of them said: The righteous women of Quraysh. And the other said: The women of Quraysh, the most affectionate toward a child in his childhood and the most careful with a husband regarding his property."
"1075","1079 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Allah, Aslam, Ghifar, Juhaynah, and Muzaynah are better than the two allies - Asad and Ghatfan - and than Banu Tamim and Banu Amir ibn Sasah. He raised his voice with it."
"1076","1080 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of Yemen have come to you; they are the most tender of hearts and the softest of hearts. Faith is Yemeni and wisdom is Yemeni, while harshness, cruelty, and hardness of hearts are among the loud-voiced owners of wool (Bedouins), at the roots of the tails of camels, from Rabiah and Mudar. Sufyan said: And he only means by his saying: The people of Yemen have come to you, the people of Tihamah, because Makkah is Yemen, and it is Tihami, and this is his saying: Faith is Yemeni and wisdom is Yemeni."
"1077","1081 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: Al-Tufayl ibn Amr al-Dawsi came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, Daws has disobeyed and refused, so supplicate against them. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) faced the qiblah and raised his hand, and the people said: Daws is ruined. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, guide Daws and bring them. Twice."
"1078","1082 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah: That a Bedouin man gifted the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a camel, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave him three (camels in return) but he was not pleased, then he gave him three more but he was not pleased, then he gave him three more, so he was pleased with the nine. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I had intended not to accept a gift except from a Qurashi, an Ansari, a Thaqafi, or a Dawsi. Sufyan said: And others besides Ibn Ajlan said: Abu Hurayrah said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this statement, he turned and saw me, so he felt shy and said: Or a Dawsi."
"1079","1083 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr narrated to us, from Tawus: That a Bedouin gave a gift to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he rewarded him but he was not pleased, then he rewarded him but he was not pleased, then he rewarded him and he was pleased. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I had intended not to accept a gift except from a Qurashi, an Ansari, or a Thaqafi."
"1080","1084 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Zaidah ibn Qudamah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed the truest verse spoken by a poet, and Ibn Abi al-Salt almost accepted Islam."
"1081","1085 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, he said: Al-Araj informed me that he heard Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman saying: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in the dawn prayer, then turned to the people with his face and said: While a man was driving a cow, it grew tired, so he rode it and struck it. It said: We were not created for this; we were only created for plowing the earth. The people said: Glory be to Allah, a cow speaks. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I believe in it, I and Abu Bakr and Umar. And they were not there. Then he said: While a man was among his sheep, a wolf pounced upon one of them, but its owner caught up and rescued it. The wolf said: Who will be for it on the day of the wild beasts, the day when it has no shepherd other than me? The people said: Glory be to Allah, a wolf speaks. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I believe in it, I and Abu Bakr and Umar. And they were not there."
"1082","1086 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Misar narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with a similar narration, except that he said: I believe in it, I and Abu Bakr and Umar."
"1083","1087 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, he said: I heard Qays saying: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: I accompanied the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for three years, and I was not more eager for anything in those years than to memorize something. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: For one of you to take his rope and gather firewood with it, then come with it upon his back and sell it, then eat from it or give it in charity, is better for him than to come to a man whom Allah has enriched from His bounty and ask him, whether he gives him or withholds from him. For indeed the upper hand is better than the lower hand."
"1084","1088 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For one of you to take his rope and gather firewood upon his back, then sell it and eat from it and give in charity, is better for him than to come to a man whom Allah has enriched and ask him, whether he gives him or withholds from him. For indeed the upper hand is better than the lower hand."
"1085","1089 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from Said, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with a similar narration, and he added in it: And begin with those you support."
"1086","1090 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: We heard from al-Hajari narrations from Abu Iyad, from Abu Hurayrah - this is one of them - who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The poor person is not the one whom a date or two dates, nor a morsel or two morsels, turn away. Rather the poor person is the one who does not beg nor is his place known so that he may be given."
"1087","1091 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A swarm of locusts of gold was sent down upon Ayyub, so he began spreading out, gathering them into his garment. He was called: O Ayyub, was what We gave you not enough for you? He said: O my Lord, who can dispense with Your bounty?"
"1088","1092 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best charity is a milch animal lent out, which goes out in the morning with a bowl of milk or returns in the evening with a bowl of milk."
"1089","1093 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with a similar narration, and he added in it: And Allah writes for him for every milking he milks a good deed - or he said: ten good deeds - according to its milking, whether it gave little or much milk."
"1090","1094 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Richness is not from abundance of possessions; rather richness is richness of the soul."
"1091","1095 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of the spender and the miser is like that of two men upon whom are two coats of armor of iron from their breasts to their collarbones. When the spender intends to spend, the coat of mail widens upon him - or passes - until it covers his fingertips and erases his tracks. And when the miser intends to spend, the coat of mail contracts upon him and every ring stays in its place until it grips his collarbone - or he said: his neck. Abu Hurayrah said: So I bear witness that I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying with his hand like this. And Sufyan gestured with his hand toward his throat, and he widens it but it does not widen. Twice."
"1092","1096 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Muslim ibn Yannaq, from Tawus, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with a similar narration, except that he said: And he widens it but it does not widen."
"1093","1097 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you sees one who is above him in wealth and physique, let him look at one who is below him in that."
"1094","1098 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah said: O son of Adam, spend and I shall spend upon you. He said: The right hand of Allah is full, overflowing, nothing diminishes it night and day."
"1095","1099 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The food of two suffices three, and the food of three suffices four."
"1096","1100 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The heart of the old man remains young in love of two things: love of wealth and love of life. And sometimes Sufyan would say: Life."
"1097","1101 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the servant of one of you suffices him the preparation of his food and endures its heat and smoke for him, let him seat him and let him eat with him. If he refuses, let him take a morsel, soak it (in broth), then give it to him."
"1098","1102 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from Said, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with a similar narration."
"1099","1103 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Khalid, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with a similar narration."
"1100","1104 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Dinar narrated to us, that he heard Sulayman ibn Yasar narrating from Irak ibn Malik, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: There is no charity upon the Muslim for his slave nor for his horse."
"1101","1105 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn Musa narrated to us, from Makhul, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Irak, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with a similar narration."
"1102","1106 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Yazid ibn Jabir narrated to us, he said: I heard Irak ibn Malik narrating from Abu Hurayrah with a similar narration, but he did not raise it (to the Prophet)."
"1103","1107 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Zuhri saying: I heard Abd al-Rahman al-Araj saying: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you seeks permission from his neighbor to fix a beam in his wall, let him not prevent him. When he narrated it to them, they lowered their heads, so he said: Why do I see you turning away? By Allah, I shall surely throw it between your shoulders. Sufyan said: I remember the place in which I heard it from al-Zuhri; he mentioned in it none but al-Araj, he did not mention Said ibn al-Musayyib in it."
"1104","1108 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, he said: Ikrimah narrated to us, he said: Shall I not inform you of brief things we heard from Abu Hurayrah? This is one of them. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you prevent his neighbor from fixing a beam in his wall. Ayyub said: If I told you that al-Hasan left much of the explanation when Ikrimah came to Basrah until he left it, I would be truthful."
"1105","1109 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If a man looks at you without permission and you throw a pebble at him and put out his eye, there is no sin upon you."
"1106","1110 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Al-Zuhri narrated to us - and he narrated to me while neither with me nor with him was anyone - he said: Said ibn al-Musayyib and Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The injury caused by a dumb animal is pardoned, the mine is pardoned, and the well is pardoned, and in buried treasure is the fifth."
"1107","1111 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with a similar narration."
"1108","1112 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not make nabidh in gourds and varnished vessels. Then Abu Hurayrah said on his own: And avoid hantam jars and naqir."
"1109","1113 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn Musa narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Said, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the slave-girl of one of you commits adultery and her adultery becomes evident, let him flog her the prescribed punishment and not rebuke her. Then if she returns and commits adultery and her adultery becomes evident, let him flog her the prescribed punishment and not rebuke her. Then if she returns and her adultery becomes evident, let him sell her even for a braid of hair - meaning a rope."
"1110","1114 - Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ziyad ibn Sad narrated to us, he heard it from Hilal ibn Abi Maymunah, narrating it from Abu Maymunah, who said: A Persian man and his wife came to Abu Hurayrah disputing over a son of theirs. The Persian said: O Abu Hurayrah, this is mature. Abu Hurayrah said: I shall surely judge between you two as I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judge: O boy, this is your father and this is your mother, so choose whichever of them you wish. Then Abu Hurayrah said: So I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a man and a woman came to him disputing over a son of theirs. The man said: O Messenger of Allah, my son draws water for me from the well of Abu Inabah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O boy, this is your father and this is your mother, so choose whichever of them you wish."
"1111","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib informed me, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: A Bedouin from Banu Fazarah came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my wife has given birth to a black boy. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you have camels? He said: Yes. He said: What are their colours? He said: Red. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Is there any greyish one among them? He said: Indeed, there are grey ones among them. He said: How did that come to them? He said: Perhaps a hereditary strain drew it out. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And this child too, perhaps a hereditary strain drew him out."
"1112","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Zuhri narrating from Sa'id [or from Abu Salamah] — one of them, or both of them; Sufyan would sometimes mention one of them alone, sometimes combine them, and sometimes express doubt, though most often he reported it from Sa'id — from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The child belongs to the marital bed, and the adulterer gets the stone."
"1113","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of suspicion, for suspicion is the most false of speech."
"1114","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has guaranteed for the one who leaves his house striving in His path, whom nothing brings out except jihad, out of faith in Me and belief in My Messenger: if I cause him to die, I shall admit him to Paradise, and if I return him, I shall return him to the house he left, attaining whatever reward or booty he attained."
"1115","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn 'Ajlan narrated to us, from one who heard Abu Hurayrah narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it, except that he said: Allah has pledged Himself. Sufyan said: And I retain the hadith of Ibn 'Ajlan more firmly."
"1116","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: And I heard Sufyan while the hadith of Ibn 'Ajlan, from al-Qa'qa', from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), was presented to him, and he approved it. Al-Humaydi said: And it was not decreed for me to ask him about it."
"1117","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three persons are under the guarantee of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic: a man who leaves his house for one of the mosques of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic; a man who goes out fighting in the path of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic; and a man who goes out to perform Hajj."
"1118","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Mis'ar narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from 'Isa ibn Talhah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The dust of the path of Allah and the smoke of Hellfire do not gather together inside a Muslim."
"1119","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No one is wounded in the path of Allah — and Allah knows best who is wounded in His path — except that he will come on the Day of Resurrection with the colour of blood and the scent of musk."
"1120","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi 'Arubah and Yahya ibn Subaykh, from Qatadah, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Bashir ibn Nahik, from Abu Hurayrah, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: If a slave is owned between two men and one of them frees his share, then if he is wealthy, the value is assessed against him; and if he has no wealth, the slave is made to work for it, without hardship being imposed on him."
"1121","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Khosrau perishes there will be no Khosrau after him, and when Caesar perishes there will be no Caesar after him. By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, their treasures will surely be spent in the path of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic."
"1122","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib informed me, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no fara' and no 'atirah. Al-Zuhri said: Al-fara' is the first offspring, and al-'atirah is a sheep slaughtered on behalf of every household in Rajab."
"1123","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, said: The son of Adam offends Me; he curses time, while I am Time; the affair is in My Hand, I alternate the night and the day."
"1124","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The son of Maryam is about to descend among you as a just judge and a just leader; he will break the cross, kill the pig, abolish the jizyah, and wealth will overflow until no one accepts it."
"1125","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: 'Imran ibn Zibyan al-Hanafi narrated to us, from a man of Banu Hanifah, who said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The son of Maryam is about to descend among you as a guiding leader and a just judge; he will break the cross, kill the pig, abolish the jizyah, and wealth will overflow until no one accepts it."
"1126","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And they say 'karam,' but true karam is the heart of the believer."
"1127","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until you fight a people whose faces are like hammered shields, and the Hour will not come until you fight a people whose shoes are of hair."
"1128","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah: They are the prominent ones. [FLAG: obscure/garbled in print]"
"1129","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until you fight a people small-eyed with flat noses."
"1130","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will come while a man is milking his she-camel, and the Hour will come while a man is plastering his trough."
"1131","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until two great factions fight each other, their claim being one."
"1132","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib: that 'Umar ibn al-Khattab passed by Hassan while he was reciting poetry in the mosque, and he glanced at him, so Hassan said: I used to recite in it while there was in it one better than you. Then he turned to Abu Hurayrah and said: I adjure you by Allah, did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Answer on my behalf; O Allah, support him with the Holy Spirit? He said: O Allah, yes."
"1133","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: al-Aqra' ibn Habis saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kissing al-Hasan or al-Husayn, may Allah be pleased with them both, and said: I have ten children and I have never kissed any of them. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed, he who does not show mercy will not be shown mercy."
"1134","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hold to this black seed, for in it is a cure for every disease except al-sam. And al-sam is death. Sufyan said: Meaning al-shuniz."
"1135","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Yasar and Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman informed me, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed, the Jews and the Christians do not dye, so differ from them."
"1136","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: 'Anbasah ibn Sa'id ibn al-'As informed me, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions at Khaybar after they had conquered it, and I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to allot me a share of the booty. One of the sons of Sa'id ibn al-'As said to him: Do not allot him a share, O Messenger of Allah. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, this is the killer of Ibn Qawqal. Then Ibn Sa'id said: How strange, a hyrax dangling down upon us from the heights of a sheep's shelter, blaming me for the killing of a Muslim man whom Allah honoured at my hands and did not disgrace me at his hands. Sufyan said: And I do not know whether he allotted him a share or not."
"1137","Sufyan said: And al-Sa'idi also narrated it to me, from his grandfather, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [FLAG: matn absent in print; isnad only]"
"1138","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of Paradise have combs of gold, and their censers are of aloeswood. Al-Humaydi said: Aloeswood is oud."
"1139","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the children of the polytheists who die young, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah knows best what they would have done."
"1140","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah the Exalted said: The vow brings nothing upon the son of Adam that I have not decreed for him, but it is something through which I extract from the miser; he brings Me through it what he would not bring Me through miserliness."
"1141","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [FLAG: matn absent in print; isnad only]"
"1142","And 'Amr narrated it to us, from Tawus, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every newborn is born upon the fitrah, then his parents make him Jewish and make him Christian. Abu al-Zinad added: And they make him Magian [or make him a polytheist]. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the children of the polytheists who die young, and he said: Allah knows best what they would have done."
"1143","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn 'Ajlan narrated to us, from a man of the family of Abu Rabi'ah, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The strong believer is better and more beloved to Allah the Exalted than the weak believer, and in each there is good. Be keen on what benefits you and do not feel helpless; if something overcomes you, say: Allah decreed, and what He willed He did; and beware of 'if,' for it opens the work of Satan."
"1144","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: 'Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Tawus, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Adam and Musa disputed. Musa said to Adam: O Adam, you are our father; you disappointed us and expelled us from Paradise. Adam said: You are Musa; Allah chose you with His speech and inscribed for you in the Tablets with His Hand; do you blame me for a matter that Allah decreed for me forty years before He created me? Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: So Adam overcame Musa."
"1145","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-A'raj, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the like of it. [FLAG: matn by reference to previous hadith]"
"1146","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: 'Umarah ibn al-Qa'qa' narrated to us, from Abu Zur'ah ibn 'Amr ibn Jarir, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: There is no contagion and no bad omen; a mangy camel makes a hundred mangy — so who infected the first?"
"1147","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: 'Umarah ibn al-Qa'qa' narrated to us, from Abu Zur'ah ibn 'Amr ibn Jarir, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Who among people is most deserving of my good companionship? He said: Your mother — twice; he said: Then who? He said: Your father. Sufyan said: So they consider two-thirds of dutifulness for the mother and one-third for the father."
"1148","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: al-Fudayl ibn 'Iyad narrated to us, from Hisham, from al-Hasan, who said: Two-thirds of dutifulness belongs to the mother and one-third to the father."
"1149","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn 'Ajlan narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you say: May Allah disgrace your face and the face of whoever resembles your face, for Allah created Adam upon his image."
"1150","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you strikes, let him avoid the face, for Allah created Adam upon his image."
"1151","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah laughs at two men, one of whom kills the other, yet both enter Paradise together: one of them is a disbeliever who kills his companion, then he accepts Islam and is martyred."
"1152","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever obeys me has obeyed Allah, and whoever obeys my commander has obeyed me."
"1153","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Surplus water is not to be withheld so that herbage is thereby withheld."
"1154","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah. [FLAG: matn absent in print; isnad only]"
"1155","And Ibn 'Ajlan, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave me with what I have left you, for those before you were destroyed only by their many questions and their differing with their prophets. What I forbid you, refrain from, and what I command you, do of it what you can. Ibn 'Ajlan added: So I narrated it to Aban ibn Salih, and he used to admire this phrase: Do of it what you can."
"1156","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah said: My mercy has preceded My anger."
"1157","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed, the most debased of names in the sight of Allah is a man named king of kings. Sufyan said: Shahanshah."
"1158","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer does not commit adultery while committing it as a believer, nor does he steal while stealing as a believer, nor does he drink wine while drinking it as a believer, nor does he plunder booty while plundering it as a believer."
"1159","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This Fire is one part of seventy parts of the Fire of Hell; it was struck with water twice, and were it not for that, no one would derive any benefit from it."
"1160","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed, Allah has ninety-nine Names, one hundred minus one; whoever preserves them will enter Paradise, and He is Odd and loves the odd."
"1161","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed, in Paradise there is a tree in whose shade a rider travels a hundred years without crossing it. So recite if you wish: And extended shade."
"1162","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will find among the worst of people the two-faced one."
"1163","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, said: I have prepared for My righteous servants what no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and what has not occurred to the heart of a human. And recite if you wish: No soul knows what is hidden for them of comfort for the eyes, as reward for what they used to do."
"1164","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My heirs do not divide a dinar; what I leave after the maintenance of my family and the provision of my workers is charity; and my heirs do not divide a dinar."
"1165","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the strap of one of you breaks, let him not walk in one sandal or one slipper until he repairs the other; and when he puts on sandals, let him begin with the right, and when he removes them, let him begin with the left; and let the right be the first to be shod and the last to be unshod."
"1166","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you not marvel at how Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, diverts from me the abuse of Quraysh and their curse? They abuse Mudhammam and curse Mudhammam, while I am Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1167","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Paradise and Hell disputed. This one said: The tyrants and the arrogant will enter me. And this one said: The weak and the poor will enter me. So Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, said to this one: You are My punishment; I punish with you whom I will. And He said to this one: You are My mercy; I show mercy with you to whom I will. Sufyan said: And I deem in it: And for each one of you will be its fill."
"1168","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to us, while he was leaning on my hands during tawaf, he said: One who heard Abu Hurayrah informed me, saying: Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you is in the shade and it recedes from him so that part of him is in the sun and part of him is in the shade, let him move away from it."
"1169","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-'Ala' narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you yawns, let him suppress it or place his hand over his mouth."
"1170","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Suhayl ibn Abi Salih narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): That a man passed by a thorny branch and removed it from the road, so he was forgiven. And Sufyan would sometimes say: So Allah thanked him and forgave him."
"1171","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani narrated to us, he said: 'Ikrimah informed us, he said: Shall I not inform you of short matters we heard from Abu Hurayrah? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade drinking from the mouth of the waterskin."
"1172","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, that he heard 'Abd al-Rahman al-A'raj saying: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: They claim that Abu Hurayrah narrates much from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Allah is the appointing authority. I was a poor man who accompanied the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for the fill of my stomach. The Ansar were occupied with tending their properties, and the Muhajirun were occupied with trading in the markets. I witnessed a gathering of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was speaking, and he said: Whoever spreads his cloak until I finish my speech, then draws it to himself, will not forget anything he heard from me. So I spread a cloak that was upon me, and when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished his speech, I drew it to myself; and by the One Who sent him with the truth, I have not forgotten anything since that I heard from him. Sufyan said: Al-Mas'udi said: And another stood and spread his cloak, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The young Dawsi has preceded you to it."
"1173","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, who said: Men differed about men and women, which of them are more in Paradise, so they came to Abu Hurayrah and asked him. He said: Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first group of my ummah to enter Paradise will be upon the image of the moon on the night of full moon; then those who follow them upon the brightest brilliant star in the sky. And Sufyan would sometimes say: Brilliant; for each one of them will be two wives, the marrow of whose shins will be seen from behind the flesh, and there is no bachelor in Paradise."
"1174","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Name yourselves with my name, but do not use my kunyah."
"1175","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you sees a dream he dislikes, let him pray two rak'ahs, and let him not inform anyone of it, for it will not harm him."
"1176","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ziyad ibn Sa'd Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Khurasani narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Ka'bah will be demolished by Dhu al-Suwayqatayn from Abyssinia."
"1177","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People are about to spur the flanks of riding camels in search of knowledge, and they will not find a scholar more knowledgeable than the scholar of Madinah."
"1178","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Hafs 'Umar ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhaysin al-Sahmi, who said: I heard Muhammad ibn Qays ibn Makhramah narrating from Abu Hurayrah, who said: When 'Whoever does evil will be recompensed for it' was revealed, that weighed heavily upon the Muslims, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Aim rightly, be upright, and receive glad tidings; for everything that befalls the Muslim is an expiation for him, even the thorn that pricks him and the stumble by which he stumbles."
"1179","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: 'Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib narrated to us, from al-Agharr, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, said: Pride is My cloak, and might is My lower garment; whoever contends with Me for either of them, I shall cast him into the Fire."
"1180","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Sa'd al-Ta'i Abu Mujahid — I heard it from him while I was a boy — from Abu Mudillah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: They said: O Messenger of Allah, when we are with you our hearts are in one state, but when we leave you they are in another state. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you were, when you leave me, as you are when you are with me, the angels would shake hands with you. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The structure of Paradise is a brick of gold and a brick of silver; its mortar is pungent musk, its pebbles are pearls, chrysolite, and ruby. And he mentioned a long hadith."
"1181","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: 'Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, he said: I heard 'Ikrimah saying: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: Indeed, the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah decrees the matter in heaven, the angels beat their wings in submission to His word, as though it were a chain upon smooth rock; and when terror is removed from their hearts, they say: What did your Lord say? They say: The truth which He spoke, and He is the Most High, the Most Great. Then the eavesdroppers hear it, the eavesdroppers being one above another. And Sufyan described some of them above others. He said: So one hears the word and casts it to the one below him, then the other casts it to the one below him, then he casts it onto the tongue of the sorcerer or the soothsayer; sometimes the shooting star reaches him before he casts it, and sometimes he casts it before it reaches him; then he lies with it a hundred lies. So it is said: Did he not tell us on such-and-such day such-and-such regarding the word heard from heaven? So he is believed because of that word heard from heaven."
"1182","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Hubab Sa'id ibn Yasar informed us, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was commanded to a town that consumes towns; they say: Yathrib, but it is Madinah; it expels people as the bellows expels the dross of iron."
"1183","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn 'Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People will keep asking until they say: This is Allah who created everything, so who created Allah? He said: So if one of you finds that, let him say: We believe in Allah."
"1184","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn 'Ajlan narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu al-Hubab Sa'id ibn Yasar saying: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, there is no servant who gives charity from lawful earnings — and Allah accepts only what is lawful, and nothing ascends to heaven except what is lawful — and places it in its right place, except that it is as though he places it in the Hand of the Most Merciful, and He nurtures it for him as one of you raises his foal or his young camel, until even the morsel or the date comes on the Day of Resurrection like a great mountain. And he recited: And He is the One Who accepts repentance from His servants and takes the charities."
"1185","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn 'Ajlan narrated to us, from Bukayr ibn 'Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj, from 'Ajlan, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The slave is entitled to his food and clothing, and he is not burdened with work except what he can bear."
"1186","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn 'Ajlan narrated to us, from Bukayr, from 'Ajlan, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We have not made peace with them since we fought them, and whoever leaves any of them out of fear is not of me — meaning snakes."
"1187","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he sneezed, would cover his face and muffle his sneeze."
"1188","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn 'Ajlan narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There are no people who sit in a gathering in which they do not remember Allah except that it will be a cause of regret for them."
"1189","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn 'Ajlan narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of obscenity, for Allah hates the obscene, foul-mouthed person; and beware of wrongdoing, for wrongdoing is darknesses on the Day of Resurrection; and beware of miserliness, for it called those before you to shed their blood, sever their kinship, and deem their sanctities lawful."
"1190","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu 'Abd al-'Aziz Musa ibn 'Ubaydah al-Rabadhi narrating from Muhammad ibn Thabit, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man says to his brother: May Allah reward you with good, he has excelled in praise."
"1191","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn 'Ajlan narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sneezing is from Allah, and yawning is from Satan; so when one of you yawns, let him place his hand over his mouth, and when he says: Hah, hah, that is only from Satan laughing in his belly. [FLAG: obscure wording rendered literally]"
"1192","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn 'Ajlan narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayrah, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When you come upon seated people, greet them, and when you rise, greet them; for the first is no more entitled than the last."
"1193","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn 'Alqamah narrated to us, from Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Four rivers are from Paradise: the Euphrates, Sayhan, Jayhan, and the Nile."
"1194","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Kathir narrated to us, from Wahb ibn Kaysan, who said: I saw Abu Hurayrah leading the people in prayer at Madinah on the evening of the first day of departure from Mina, then he said: Indeed, Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has preceded with good deeds, and indeed Dhakwan, the freed slave of Marwan, has preceded the pilgrims, and he has reported about the people in safety. Sufyan said: And Dhakwan said: I burdened myself with it. [FLAG: obscure/garbled ending rendered literally]"
"1195","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn 'Alqamah narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Narrate from the Children of Israel, and there is no harm; narrate from me, but do not lie about me."
"1196","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, and countless persons narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"1197","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu Harun Musa ibn Abi 'Isa al-Madini the tailor narrated to us, that he heard Abu 'Abd Allah al-Qarrazz saying: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any tyrant who intends the people of Madinah with evil, Allah will melt him in the Fire as salt melts in water; and no one endures its hardship and severity except that I shall be a witness — or an intercessor — for him on the Day of Resurrection."
"1198","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed, woman was created from a rib; she will never be straight for you upon one way. If you enjoy her, you enjoy her while crookedness is in her; and if you go to straighten her, you break her, and her breaking is her divorce."
"1199","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: 'Imran ibn Zibyan al-Hanafi narrated to us, that he heard a man of Banu Hanifah saying: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: I went with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to the Jews of Banu Qaynuqa' to study with them, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man smeared with perfume, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, perhaps he is a bridegroom. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Go, wash it off, then scrub it, then wash it, then scrub it, then wash it, then scrub it. [FLAG: lacuna in print; wording partly garbled, rendered literally]"
"1200","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ziyad ibn Sa'd narrated to us, he said: I heard Thabit al-A'raj narrating from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The worst food is the food of the wedding feast: those who come to it are barred from it, and those who dislike it are invited to it; and whoever does not answer the invitation has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."
